                "type": "text",
                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/consistency/checks_crud.py, lines 1-91\n1: \"\"\"Whether the operations a component claims are actually provided by a method.\n2: \n3: `components.crud_services` says which operations each entity supports, and\n4: nothing checked that any method provides them: the operations were validated\n5: for spelling only, against a five-word list. Measured on the corpus, every\n6: entity that declares `delete` has no method for it — inventory's two\n7: repositories and library's four all declare `delete` and none of them can\n8: delete anything.\n9: \n10: The check is confined to the two operations whose names map unambiguously onto\n11: methods: `create` (a method named create_*/add_*/insert_*/save_*), and `delete`\n12: (delete_*/remove_*/drop_*). `read_one` and `read_all` share prefixes with each\n13: other and with domain queries, and `update` is routinely folded into a create —\n14: so those three are left alone rather than guessed at, which is why the rule\n15: under-reports rather than over-reports.\n16: \"\"\"\n17: \n18: from kernel.consistency.methods import collect_methods\n19: from kernel.consistency.naming import normalize, strip_role_suffix\n20: \n21: # The method-name prefixes that implement each operation.\n22: OP_PREFIXES = {\n23:     \"create\": (\"create\", \"add\", \"insert\", \"save\", \"new\", \"make\", \"register\"),\n24:     \"delete\": (\"delete\", \"remove\", \"drop\", \"destroy\", \"discard\"),\n25: }\n26: \n27: \n28: def check_crud_coverage(components, documents, report):\n29:     \"\"\"Report each claimed operation that no reachable method implements.\"\"\"\n30:     if not isinstance(components, dict):\n31:         return\n32:     crud_services = components.get(\"crud_services\")\n33:     if not isinstance(crud_services, list):\n34:         return\n35: \n36:     for entry in crud_services:\n37:         if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n38:             continue\n39:         entity = entry.get(\"entity\")\n40:         operations = entry.get(\"operations\")\n41:         if not isinstance(entity, str) or not isinstance(operations, list):\n42:             continue\n43: \n44:         methods = _methods_for(entity, documents)\n45:         if not methods:\n46:             # No repository is reachable for this entity, so there is nothing to\n47:             # compare against; `no_repository` already covers that case.\n48:             continue\n49: \n50:         for operation in operations:\n51:             prefixes = OP_PREFIXES.get(operation)\n52:             if prefixes is None:\n53:                 continue\n54:             if any(name.lower().startswith(prefixes) for name in methods):\n55:                 continue\n56:             report.warning(\n57:                 \"unmet_crud_operation\",\n58:                 f\"components.crud_services: '{entity}' declares '{operation}' but no method \"\n59:                 f\"of {sorted(methods)} does it\",\n60:             )\n61: \n62: \n63: def _methods_for(entity, documents):\n64:     \"\"\"Every method declared for `entity`, from its repository or its services.\"\"\"\n65:     names = set()\n66:     wanted = normalize(entity)\n67: \n68:     services = documents.get(\"service_contracts\")\n69:     if isinstance(services, list):\n70:         for service in services:\n71:             if not isinstance(service, dict) or not service.get(\"service_name\"):\n72:                 continue\n73:             if strip_role_suffix(service[\"service_name\"]) == wanted:\n74:                 names |= _declared_names(service)\n75: \n76:     ports = documents.get(\"persistence_ports\")\n77:     repositories = ports.get(\"repositories\") if isinstance(ports, dict) else None\n78:     if isinstance(repositories, list):\n79:         for repository in repositories:\n80:             if isinstance(repository, dict) and normalize(repository.get(\"entity\")) == wanted:\n81:                 names |= _declared_names(repository)\n82: \n83:     return names\n84: \n85: \n86: def _declared_names(container):\n87:     return {\n88:         method[\"name\"]\n89:         for method in collect_methods(container)\n90:         if isinstance(method.get(\"name\"), str) and method[\"name\"].strip()\n91:     }"
