                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/consistency/checks_contracts.py, lines 1-43\n1: \"\"\"Consistency checks for the service contracts.\n2: \n3: Every method block is validated through kernel.consistency.methods; this module\n4: adds the service-level checks (unique, non-empty service names).\n5: \"\"\"\n6: \n7: from kernel.consistency.methods import check_method_list, is_missing, is_placeholder\n8: \n9: \n10: def check_service_contracts(services, report):\n11:     \"\"\"Validate service_contracts: service names plus every method block.\"\"\"\n12:     if services is None:\n13:         return\n14:     if not services:\n15:         # A note, not an error: a program with no domain entities has no\n16:         # services, and that is a correct answer rather than a failed step. The\n17:         # contradictory case is caught in checks_components.\n18:         report.note(\"empty_section\", \"service_contracts: list is empty\")\n19:         return\n20: \n21:     seen = set()\n22:     for service in services:\n23:         if not isinstance(service, dict):\n24:             report.error(\"invalid_value\", \"service_contracts: an entry is not an object\")\n25:             continue\n26:         name = service.get(\"service_name\")\n27:         if is_missing(name) or is_placeholder(name):\n28:             report.error(\"invalid_identifier\", \"service_contracts: a service has no service_name\")\n29:             continue\n30:         if name.strip().lower() in seen:\n31:             report.warning(\"duplicate_entry\", f\"service_contracts: service '{name}' is declared more than once\")\n32:         seen.add(name.strip().lower())\n33: \n34:     check_methods(services, report)\n35: \n36: \n37: def check_methods(services, report):\n38:     \"\"\"Validate the method block of every declared service.\"\"\"\n39:     for service in services:\n40:         if not isinstance(service, dict):\n41:             continue\n42:         label = service.get(\"service_name\") or \"<unnamed service>\"\n43:         check_method_list(service.get(\"methods\"), f\"service_contracts: {label}\", report)"
