          "type": "text",
          "text": "Readiness assessment: `probe_readiness.py` is not complete. It proves less than a generator needs.\n\nCurrent state (verified by execution):\n\n* `probe_readiness.py:191-202`: 2 blockers total, both in `expenses` (`Category op 'create'`, `Budget op 'create'` has no method of its own). 5/7 prompts report 0.\n* `check_consistency.py` on same `out/`: 0 errors, 4 warnings (2x `missing_command`, 2x `unmet_crud_operation`), 39 notes.\n\nWhat the probe does (6 families, `probe_readiness.py:103-188`): command->method by stem, adapter->service/method/param existence, crud op has own method, repo->mapping + pk-is-field, non-empty return/param name/type, raises registered.\n\nWhat's left:\n\n1. Prompt compliance missing: probe never reads `requirements.txt`. Misses `kernel/consistency/checks_surface.py:44-104` `missing_command`:\n   * `expenses`: requirements name `expense add`, surface declares `category,export,list,recurring,report` — invisible to probe.\n   * `library`: requirements name `member (add,history,list)`, surface declares only `book` — probe says `library 0 blockers`.\n   Generator would omit required surface and probe would pass.\n\n2. Adapter checks partial vs `kernel/consistency/checks_adapters.py`: probe only checks param existence (`probe_readiness.py:140-144`). Missing `misplaced_field` (e.g. `add_expense: category_id->data`, `update_budget: month->budget`), `mismatched_transform` (`DECIMAL_TO_CENTS`/`CSV_LIST`/`ISO_DATE` on wrong names), `LOOKUP_ID` without/with `lookup_entity`, unknown `lookup_entity`, bad `transform` enum, non-bool `required`, duplicate fields. All emit wrong code.\n\n3. Stem tables drifted: `probe_readiness.py:27-48` `VERB_STEMS`/`OP_STEMS` duplicate instead of importing `kernel/consistency/checks_surface.py:150-171` `COMMAND_VERB_STEMS` and `kernel/consistency/checks_crud.py:22-25` `OP_PREFIXES`. Probe lacks `export,borrow,return,history,show,remove,detect,assign,renew`; `OP_STEMS` uses substring (`stem in method`) vs checker's prefix, and `entity_methods()` (`probe_readiness.py:80-96`) uses `entity in name` substring vs `strip_role_suffix` exact — over-matches and hides blockers (e.g. `get_expenses_by_category` satisfies `read_one` via `get`).\n\n4. Method/type contract weak vs `kernel/consistency/methods.py:52-141`: probe checks non-empty only. Missing duplicate methods/params, `missing_parameters` (`create()`/`get_by_id` with no params), placeholder set incomplete (`null,nil,todo,tbd,undefined`), empty method lists, option/positional types outside `str,int,float,bool,list` (`kernel/consistency/checks_components.py:31`), unknown return/param type vocabulary.\n\n5. Persistence/model gaps vs `checks_models.py`, `checks_persistence.py`, `checks_components.py`, `checks_interfaces.py`: probe doesn't check FK target entity/field + `relationship` enum, model duplicates/PK missing/nullable/non-unique, `table` missing/duplicate, `primary_key_mismatch`, `crud entity unknown/class-name`, `no_repository`, `inconsistent_interface` (`service_contracts` vs `persistence_ports` same `XxxRepository` different methods — adapters target one, generator implements the other), `persistence.required` vs `technology` contradiction, `required=true` + empty `crud_services` (invents schema). Also silent pass when `persistence_ports.json` absent (`probe_readiness.py:51-56` returns `None->{}`).\n\n6. Errors partial vs `kernel/consistency/checks_errors.py`: probe misses `duplicate_error_subject` (`CategoryNotFound`+`MissingCategory` → 2 classes, 1 condition), `unreachable_error`, `contradictory_raise` (`create_X` raises `XNotFound`), bad `base`, empty `raises` entries.\n\n7. Consistency/determinism not measured (your \"same JSON per prompt\" requirement): probe ignores `missing_pattern` (8 notes, e.g. `add_expense`, `export_to_csv` = `NO_PATTERN_IN_DOMAIN` → generator invents body), `corrected_claim`, `low_confidence` (<0.2), `narrow_margin` (13 notes → rerun may differ).\n\n8. Engineering: no tests for probe itself (`tests/test_generator_readiness_rules.py` tests checker rules only), no exit code/CI gate (`main()` always 0), no `--dirs` parity with `check_consistency.py:28-44`.\n\nNeeded before generator: add requirements-coverage check, reuse `ServiceIndex`/adapter/invariant/pattern checks from `kernel.consistency` instead of reimplementing stems, tighten to prefix+role-suffix semantics, add interface-agreement + FK/PK/type-vocabulary + error-subject checks, surface pattern/margin signals, add tests + non-zero exit on blockers.",
