        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Yes — someone has to decide. The honest point is that the ambiguity is in the requirements text itself, not just the classifier. Examples from the current outputs:\n\n**`narrow_margin` (a rerun could record the other answer):**\n\n* `library`: *\"Book.available_copies must not exceed the number of copies added for that Book\"* — `BUDGET_OVERFLOW_GUARD` (0.376) vs `QUOTA_CAPACITY_GUARD`, margin **0.0023**. The sentence genuinely sits between \"budget overflow\" and \"capacity quota\"; no classifier can separate what the text doesn't separate.\n* `60`: *`cancel_order`* — domain `SERVICE_GUARD` beat `STANDARD_CRUD` by 0.06, and inside, `STOCK_SUFFICIENCY_GUARD` vs `BUDGET_OVERFLOW_GUARD`. Releasing reserved stock on cancel really is guard-like *and* CRUD-like.\n* `gui`: *\"A StorageLocation cannot be deleted if it has any wines assigned\"* — `STATE_TRANSITION_GUARD` vs `QUOTA_CAPACITY_GUARD` by 0.097.\n\n**`low_confidence` (< 0.2, both stages unsure):**\n\n* `60`: *`get_product_by_category_and_month(...) → List[Product]`* at **0.033**, also near-tied (`FILTER_BY_FIELD` vs `FILTER_WITH_PAGINATION` by 0.022). Description says \"grouped by\" (aggregate language) but returns records — the text contradicts itself.\n* `expenses`: *`detect_recurring() → List[Expense]`* at **0.14**, same tie. \"Detecting\" is neither filtering nor paginating language.\n\n**On \"someone must decide\":** deferring to the generator is legitimate, for three reasons:\n\n1. The generator has *more* evidence than the classifier did: raw text + signature (params, return type) + both candidates with margins. `get_product_by_category_and_month` takes no pagination params → plain filter, tie resolved from the signature alone.\n2. Most ties are code-identical. `STANDARD_CRUD` vs `REPO_QUERY` (`borrow_book`, `confirm_order`, `create_budget`) generates the same plain method either way — the tie is cosmetically undecided but operationally decided.\n3. The tie is recorded explicitly (`decision: undecided`, both alternatives, margins) instead of hidden behind a fake-confident winner. The generator rule can be: *when `undecided`, either candidate satisfies; reason from the text at temperature 0.*\n\nThe residual risk is run-to-run variance on the few ties that change the body (`BUDGET_OVERFLOW` vs `QUOTA_CAPACITY` — and note that pair recurred twice, which is exactly the signal for which pattern/description to sharpen next, without adding catalog entries now).",
          "state": {
            "itemId": "msg_01a12f44230a7110a1a298dba2c9be92"
          }
        }
