                "text": "directives across 7 prompts: {'pattern': 131, 'rule': 11, 'llm-gap': 6}\n---- rendered gap context ----\nMethod: export_expenses_to_csv(file_path: str, start_date: Optional[str], end_date: Optional[str], category_id: Optional[int], payment_method: Optional[str]) -> None: Exports filtered expenses to a CSV file.\nReturns: None\nEntity Expense: id, amount_cents, description, expense_date, category_id, payment_method, is_recurring\nIntentions:\n- Design and implement a database schema for expense tracking with models for **Category**, **Expense**, and **Budget** using SQLite with foreign keys and constraints\n- Create repositories for **ExpenseRepository**, **CategoryRepository**, and **BudgetRepository** with CRUD operations and filtering capabilities\n- Implement a **ExpenseService** with business logic for expense management, reporting, and recurring expense detection\n- Develop a **CLI interface** using the `click` library for interactive expense tracking operations\n- Handle monetary values as integers (cents) for precision, with conversion utilities for display purposes\n- Define custom exceptions for error handling (e.g., `CategoryNotFoundError`, `ExpenseNotFoundError`, `BudgetExceededException`)\nInvariants:\n- Expense.category_id must reference an existing Category\nRefused pattern FILTER_WITH_PAGINATION: FILTER_WITH_PAGINATION returns collection, but this method returns none (None)\nSame-service methods and their patterns:\n- list_expenses(category_id: Optional[int], start_date: Optional[str], end_date: Optional[str], payment_method: Optional[str]) -> List[Expense]: Lists all expenses with optional filters for category, date range, and payment method. -> FILTER_BY_FIELD\n- read_one_expense(id: int) -> Expense: Reads a single expense by its ID. -> STANDARD_CRUD\n- read_all_expenses() -> List[Expense]: Reads all expenses. -> READ_ALL\n- update_expense(id: int, data: Expense) -> Expense: Updates an expense by its ID. -> STANDARD_CRUD\n- 