        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Done — 411 tests, state unchanged (9 blockers, 0 open ties). To your question:\n\n**No — not re-asked every time.** That would charge you 3 questions per run for zero benefit when nothing changed, and break unattended runs entirely. Instead, each decision is now stamped with the prompt hash, and the extractor only honors it while the prompt stands:\n\n* `review_ties.py` stamps new records with `sha256(out/requirements.txt)`.\n* `extract_arch.py` passes the run's requirements into `apply_decisions`; a record stamped under different words is **dropped with a log line** (`predates a prompt change — dropped, will be re-asked`), the tie reopens, the probe counts it open.\n* Whitespace-normalized on both sides (stdin is stripped, the archived file isn't — without that they'd never agree).\n\nYour 3 existing records are **grandfathered without stamps** — stated openly, not silently: there's nothing to compare them against, and backfilling today's hash onto them would wrongly validate answers given under older words. Since `prompts/` is currently restored to ~the text they were decided under, they keep applying correctly; the next prompt edit that touches their context will *not* auto-invalidate them, which is the one residual gap — closing it means re-answering those 3 under hashes, a 1-minute review whenever you want it.\n\nSame design will carry the field-alias file when we build it: judgment recorded once, honored exactly while its context stands, re-asked otherwise.",
