          "type": "text",
          "text": "Locked in:\n\n* **Human-in-the-loop is the product**, not scaffolding toward automation. I'll stop designing around unattended operation — questions surface by default, nothing important auto-accepts.\n* **Ask-when-needed** = the hash gate as built: same prompt → silent; changed prompt → tie reopens, probe counts it, review asks. Perfs work stays parked.\n* Legacy records keep applying until their context demonstrably shifts; any re-answer stamps them going forward.\n\nThat makes the alias file the natural next piece — same shape as ties (`{action, field, flag}` + prompt hash), reviewed the same way — covering the 7 field mappings (`file_path`, `recurring`×2, `copies`, `book_id`, `membership_date`, whole-object `update_book`) plus the 3 already-open human calls (`stock`, 60 search UX). Say the word and I build it, then run the triage session.",
