          "type": "text",
          "text": "Built and dry-run. 425 tests green. The alias loop is ready for your separate triage session:\n\n* **`review_aliases.py OUT_DIR`** (or `--list` to preview) — asks only pairs no rule can reach, showing action, target, bound leaves, declared flags, and numbered suggestions. Answers persist to `field_aliases.json` (prompt-hash stamped like decisions), patch the on-disk adapters immediately, and re-apply on every future run.\n* **`extract_arch.py`** applies them post-run, same position as decisions. Probe and generator needed zero changes — renamed fields just pass the existing rules.\n\nPreview of what's waiting for you (`--list` output):\n\n* **expenses (1):** `export_to_csv.file_path` → leaf `expense export` declares *no flags at all* — note this: aliasing alone can't unblock it, the leaf needs `--output` first (surface-side, a rerun after the alias won't help; flag it to me if you want the one-of... rather, tell me and I'll look at the leaf).\n* **library (2):** `add_book.copies` (leaf flags exist: author_id/copies/isbn/… — answerable) and whole-object `update_book.book` (no bound leaf — answerable only by drop/decompose, i.e. LLM-or-you territory disguised as a mapping).\n* **60 (2):** `customer_id`/`order_id` — bound leaves exist but declare no flags. Same story as export: mapping without a flag changes nothing; these two genuinely need surface flags (prompt) or dropped adapters.\n* **inventory (1):** `stock_qty` — flags exist around it but none matches; this is really your required-vs-optional call wearing a mapping costume.\n\nSo triage honestly: `copies` is the one clean mapping; the rest will each tell you what *else* they need when you see their leaves. Run `python review_aliases.py out/<prompt>` whenever ready — skips leave everything open, nothing half-applied.",
