        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two answers:\n\n1. **`extract_archi.py` no longer exists** — you had me rename it to `extract_arch.py` earlier (`git mv`, references updated). Same CLI otherwise:\n   `python extract_arch.py --model ../models/<name>.gguf --output out/<prompt> < prompts/prompt_*.txt`\n   plus `--from-step <step>` for resumes and `--check` for the consistency report.\n\n2. **No — `extract_arch` never asks anything.** It *applies* existing `field_aliases.json`/`decisions.json` (re-recording them into fresh output), but open pairs stay open: the probe reports them, `review_aliases.py` / `review_ties.py` ask them. That's deliberate per your own split — extraction stays batch-safe (background runs, no stdin hijack), triage stays a separate, deliberate session.\n\nIf you want one command for the attended case, I can add `--review`: run extraction, then drop into both reviews interactively when anything is open, then re-probe. Say the word — otherwise the current division stands: `extract_arch.py` → `probe_readiness.py` → `review_*.py` → rerun.",
