        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One entry point, as specified. 433 tests green, probe unchanged at 9/0-open:\n\n**`extract_arch.py --requirements prompts/prompt_X.txt --chat`** now runs the full attended loop: extract → write → probe → tie review (only if open ties) → alias review (only if open pairs) → re-probe with the remaining count as the exit code.\n\nDesign decisions worth knowing:\n\n* **Each review runs only when its questions exist.** Clean output asks nothing — verified by test.\n* **Structural blockers are reported, never asked.** No typed answer fixes a missing command or an unsuppliable field; those need reruns or code, so chat lists them and moves on.\n* **`--chat` refuses piped stdin** (`--requirements` required). Questions arrive over stdin — a pipe would EOF every answer into a silent skip, the worst possible failure for an attended tool. This is enforced with exit 2, not documented hopefully.\n* **Plumbing is testable without the model**: `resolve_requirements` (file/stdin/empty/missing) and `chat_flow` (mocked runners) are pinned; the model boundary stays where it was.\n\nUsage going forward:\n```\npython extract_arch.py --model ../models/<m>.gguf --output out/<p> --requirements prompts/prompt_<p>.txt --chat\n```\nYour separate triage session is now just this command on the four blocked prompts — answers land in `decisions.json`/`field_aliases.json` and apply to every later run while their prompts stand.",
