        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Three precise asks: list existing fields, offer creation, and why not auto-add. The last one first, because it governs the design: auto-adding a schema field requires inventing its type, nullability, and foreign key. Sometimes that's derivable (flag type `int` + `LOOKUP_ID` + `lookup_entity: Author`), usually it isn't — and a wrong guess corrupts storage silently. So: system infers and *offers* creation as a one-keystroke choice (with its derivation shown), you confirm, it applies. No silent schema writes, ever.",
