        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Not the whole directory — but record files alone aren't enough either, because the *documents* were patched too (renamed fields, created model field, decided entries). Two precise options:\n\n**Clean re-ask (recommended):** fresh docs + no records, so every question reopens as first seen:\n```\ncp -r out/library backup/out_library_answered   # keep your answered state\nrm out/library/decisions.json out/library/field_aliases.json\npython extract_arch.py --model ../models/<m>.gguf --output out/library \\\n    --requirements prompts/prompt_library_system.txt\npython review_aliases.py out/library            # or add --chat above instead\n```\nThe rerun regenerates pristine docs (temp-0 → essentially identical to what you triaged), and with no record files every pair reopens. Or `rm -rf out/library` first — equivalent, since the run rewrites everything except the two record files (which is exactly why they need separate deletion).\n\n**Why not just delete the record files:** the patched docs would stay silent — e.g. `copies` is already `available_copies` on disk, so there's no pair left to ask about. Records suppress *re-asking*, patches suppress *the question itself*. You need both layers reset, which is what a fresh run does.\n\nSame shape for any prompt. And with temp-0 determinism, the fresh run reproduces the same questions — good for verifying the improved review text against what confused you before.",
