        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Fixed at the root cause, not the symptom. What your log shows:\n\n1. **First crash** (`llama_decode -3` in classifier decode) — the known transient Metal flake.\n2. **Retry then failed with \"Failed to load model\"** although the file exists — because the retry reloaded *in-process*, beside the still-loaded extractor and the half-dead classifier. GPU pressure, not a missing file. My in-process retry design poisoned its own well.\n\nThe fix, now in `extract_arch.py` (469 tests green):\n\n* **Resume rounds run as child processes** (`resume_in_subprocess`): clean Metal state every attempt, logs streaming live, and anything a crash leaves behind dies with the child — the snapshot still decides what survives. A second consecutive failure still rolls back and reports.\n* Crash paths now print the evidence snapshot location instead of swallowing it.\n* I also removed the leftover `.chat_snapshot_library` from your crashed session (verified byte-identical to the rolled-back state first).\n\nSo to your \"continue without failure\": the next `--chat` run retries the library resume in a fresh process, where the pressure that killed attempt 2 cannot exist. If *that* crashes too, it rolls back to your 2 blockers with the evidence path printed — the session ends informed, never corrupted.",
          "state": {
            "itemId": "msg_01a135ac8ef47062959d5944a2f648ea"
          }
        }
