          "text": "Here it is — the exact system prompt, reconstructed through the same code path (above is verbatim; the run's entity block and archived requirements are byte-identical inputs). The two sentences that already demand precisely what's missing:\n\n> *\"Every command line the requirements list must appear in the surface, and each distinct thing the requirements act on is a command of its own: if they name 'book add', 'book list', 'book search', **'member add', 'member list' and 'borrow', the surface declares both 'book' and 'member' as commands, and 'borrow' as a command in its own right** — never as a subcommand of whichever thing was written first, and **never omitted**.\"*\n\n> *\"A line whose form is '\\<program\\> \\<verb\\> --flag', with a single word between the program name and the first flag, **makes that word a top-level command** carrying its own options.\"*\n\nThe instruction could not be more explicit — it names `member` and `borrow` nearly literally. The model dropped them anyway, then dropped them again on the retry that named them. So to your hallucination-vs-bug question, this is the exhibit: **instruction-following failure, not underspecification and not a pipeline defect.** (Plausible mechanism, stated as hypothesis only: the command list is item 10 of a ~1,600-word prompt, and small models dilute long instructions — but I can't observe attention, only the omission.)\n\nYour options from here, cheapest first:\n\n1. **Command-level repair** (my recommendation): extend the flag-repair philosophy one level up — synthesize missing commands from the requirements' own backtick lines (`member` + `add`/`history` + flags typed from the models, exactly like the flag repair already does). Every element grounded, logged, tested. It converts this whole failure class from rerun-luck into deterministic output.\n2. **Hot rerun** (`--temperature 0.7` — the lever I held back): new roll, may recover `member`, may scramble something else; gate judges.\n3. **Prompt surgery** (shorten/restructure, move the coverage demand last): still frozen per your directive; say the word if you want it.\n\nWant the command repair built?",
