          "type": "text",
          "text": "Verdict: **partial yes** — the checklist moved the needle, but it's not enforcement. Itemized:\n\n**Healed by this run (mechanism works):**\n* `member` command exists again with `add`/`list` (was entirely missing) — the enumerated lines did exactly their job.\n* `book/add` flags repaired in-pipeline (`--isbn`, `--copies` etc.).\n* Coverage retry healed 3→2 and keep-best kept the better doc.\n* Previous unknowns (`copies`, `author_id`, `membership_date`, `book_loan_history`) all gone.\n\n**Still blocked (5), all structural mis-modeling the checklist didn't prevent:**\n* `member` lacks `history` — listed line 9, still dropped.\n* `borrow`/`return` nest `member-id`/`loan-id` as *subcommands* instead of flags (plus the collision-guard correctly refusing to duplicate them), and `overdue` grew an invented `member_history` subcommand — the model reshuffles structure around the checklist rather than following it.\n\nSo the enumerated block fixes *omission* (member recovered) but not *mis-structuring* (nesting/invention persist) — and the probe caught every bit of it, nothing silent. The remaining failure is one level up from what we built for: the model doesn't just drop lines, it reinterprets their shape.\n\nTwo paths from here: (a) rerun again — variance demonstrably moves structure between rolls, and the gate keeps score; (b) the deterministic endgame I flagged earlier — synthesize the mechanical 90% (commands/subs/flags from the parsed lines, which the checker already proves parseable) and leave the model only shorts, `crud_services`, and judgment calls. (b) is the bigger build but it's the only one that *guarantees* rather than *urges*. Which way?",
