            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/extraction/dedupe.py, lines 1-60\n1: \"\"\"Deterministic removal of exactly repeated names from a generated document.\n2: \n3: The grammars close the *entity* names, but a method name is free text, and GBNF\n4: cannot express \"a list of distinct strings\": distinctness over an unbounded\n5: alphabet is not a regular property, so no grammar can forbid a repeat. A model\n6: that starts repeating a name therefore keeps going, and only the list-length cap\n7: stops it — which is not a fix, because a cap low enough to cut a loop is also\n8: low enough to truncate a legitimate long list.\n9: \n10: So the repeat is removed after generation instead, and only ever the repeat: the\n11: first occurrence of a name is kept exactly as the model wrote it and later\n12: occurrences of the same name in the same list are dropped. Nothing is renamed,\n13: rewritten or invented, so this cannot change what a document says — it removes\n14: entries that say the same thing twice.\n15: \n16: Measured cause: cli_tool's ProductRepository listed `order_items` four times and\n17: `orders`, `products`, `getOrderStats` three times each, after nine genuine\n18: methods — the model enumerating the other entities of the names block and never\n19: deciding to stop. Duplicates appeared only there, in one of seven prompts.\n20: \"\"\"\n21: \n22: def deduplicate(key, body):\n23:     \"\"\"Drop exact duplicate names from `body`, returning (body, removed count).\n24: \n25:     `body` is the parsed document (the value under `key`), or None.\n26:     \"\"\"\n27:     if key == \"service_contracts\":\n28:         return _deduplicate_services(body)\n29:     if key == \"persistence_ports\":\n30:         return _deduplicate_ports(body)\n31:     if key == \"components\":\n32:         return _deduplicate_components(body)\n33:     return body, 0\n34: \n35: \n36: def _deduplicate_components(components):\n37:     \"\"\"Drop repeated command and subcommand names from the CLI surface.\n38: \n39:     Same defect, same shape as the method repeats this module already handles:\n40:     library listed `member` twice, once with `[add, list]` and once with\n41:     `[history]`. A CLI framework would refuse the second registration, so the\n42:     repeat is a document that cannot become a program. Only an exact repeat is\n43:     removed — `member` and `Member` are left for the checker to report, because\n44:     deciding those name one command is an interpretation and this module makes\n45:     none.\n46:     \"\"\"\n47:     if not isinstance(components, dict):\n48:         return components, 0\n49:     facade = components.get(\"facade\")\n50:     if not isinstance(facade, dict):\n51:         return components, 0\n52:     invocation = facade.get(\"invocation\")\n53:     if not isinstance(invocation, dict):\n54:         return components, 0\n55: \n56:     options, removed = _deduplicate_by_name(invocation.get(\"options\"))\n57:     invocation[\"options\"] = options\n58:     commands, count = _deduplicate_by_name(invocation.get(\"commands\"))\n59:     invocation[\"commands\"] = commands\n60:     removed += count\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"
