            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/extraction/dedupe.py, lines 1-225\n1: \"\"\"Deterministic removal of exactly repeated names from a generated document.\n2: \n3: The grammars close the *entity* names, but a method name is free text, and GBNF\n4: cannot express \"a list of distinct strings\": distinctness over an unbounded\n5: alphabet is not a regular property, so no grammar can forbid a repeat. A model\n6: that starts repeating a name therefore keeps going, and only the list-length cap\n7: stops it — which is not a fix, because a cap low enough to cut a loop is also\n8: low enough to truncate a legitimate long list.\n9: \n10: So the repeat is removed after generation instead, and only ever the repeat: the\n11: first occurrence of a name is kept exactly as the model wrote it and later\n12: occurrences of the same name in the same list are dropped. Nothing is renamed,\n13: rewritten or invented, so this cannot change what a document says — it removes\n14: entries that say the same thing twice.\n15: \n16: Measured cause: cli_tool's ProductRepository listed `order_items` four times and\n17: `orders`, `products`, `getOrderStats` three times each, after nine genuine\n18: methods — the model enumerating the other entities of the names block and never\n19: deciding to stop. Duplicates appeared only there, in one of seven prompts.\n20: \"\"\"\n21: \n22: def deduplicate(key, body):\n23:     \"\"\"Drop exact duplicate names from `body`, returning (body, removed count).\n24: \n25:     `body` is the parsed document (the value under `key`), or None.\n26:     \"\"\"\n27:     if key == \"service_contracts\":\n28:         return _deduplicate_services(body)\n29:     if key == \"persistence_ports\":\n30:         return _deduplicate_ports(body)\n31:     if key == \"components\":\n32:         return _deduplicate_components(body)\n33:     return body, 0\n34: \n35: \n36: def _deduplicate_components(components):\n37:     \"\"\"Drop repeated command and subcommand names from the CLI surface.\n38: \n39:     Same defect, same shape as the method repeats this module already handles:\n40:     library listed `member` twice, once with `[add, list]` and once with\n41:     `[history]`. A CLI framework would refuse the second registration, so the\n42:     repeat is a document that cannot become a program. Only an exact repeat is\n43:     removed — `member` and `Member` are left for the checker to report, because\n44:     deciding those name one command is an interpretation and this module makes\n45:     none.\n46:     \"\"\"\n47:     if not isinstance(components, dict):\n48:         return components, 0\n49:     facade = components.get(\"facade\")\n50:     if not isinstance(facade, dict):\n51:         return components, 0\n52:     invocation = facade.get(\"invocation\")\n53:     if not isinstance(invocation, dict):\n54:         return components, 0\n55: \n56:     options, removed = _deduplicate_by_name(invocation.get(\"options\"))\n57:     invocation[\"options\"] = options\n58:     commands, count = _deduplicate_by_name(invocation.get(\"commands\"))\n59:     invocation[\"commands\"] = commands\n60:     removed += count\n61:     for command in commands or []:\n62:         if not isinstance(command, dict):\n63:             continue\n64:         command_options, count = _deduplicate_by_name(command.get(\"options\"))\n65:         command[\"options\"] = command_options\n66:         removed += count\n67:         subcommands, count = _deduplicate_by_name(command.get(\"subcommands\"))\n68:         command[\"subcommands\"] = subcommands\n69:         removed += count\n70:         for subcommand in subcommands or []:\n71:             if not isinstance(subcommand, dict):\n72:                 continue\n73:             subcommand_options, count = _deduplicate_by_name(subcommand.get(\"options\"))\n74:             subcommand[\"options\"] = subcommand_options\n75:             removed += count\n76:     return components, removed\n77: \n78: \n79: def _deduplicate_by_name(items):\n80:     \"\"\"Keep the first item of each exact `name`; drop later ones.\"\"\"\n81:     if not isinstance(items, list):\n82:         return items, 0\n83:     kept = []\n84:     seen = set()\n85:     removed = 0\n86:     for item in items:\n87:         if not isinstance(item, dict):\n88:             kept.append(item)\n89:             continue\n90:         name = item.get(\"name\")\n91:         if isinstance(name, str) and name in seen:\n92:             removed += 1\n93:             continue\n94:         if isinstance(name, str):\n95:             seen.add(name)\n96:         kept.append(item)\n97:     return kept, removed\n98: \n99: \n100: def _deduplicate_services(services):\n101:     \"\"\"Merge services that share a name, then drop repeated method names.\n102: \n103:     The model sometimes emits one service per *group* of methods — 60 produced\n104:     `CategoryRepository` twice and `OrderService` three times — which says the\n105:     same thing as one entry holding all those methods, and a second registration\n106:     of a name is what a program cannot have. Merging keeps the first spelling and\n107:     the order of first appearance — nothing is renamed or invented — and the\n108:     methods are then deduplicated by name, because the two entries may both have\n109:     declared one.\n110:     \"\"\"\n111:     if not isinstance(services, list):\n112:         return services, 0\n113:     merged = []\n114:     opened = {}\n115:     removed = 0\n116:     for service in services:\n117:         if not isinstance(service, dict):\n118:             merged.append(service)\n119:             continue\n120:         name = service.get(\"service_name\")\n121:         key = name.strip().lower() if isinstance(name, str) else None\n122:         if key is not None and key in opened:\n123:             existing = opened[key]\n124:             combined = (existing.get(\"methods\") or []) + (service.get(\"methods\") or [])\n125:             existing[\"methods\"] = combined\n126:             removed += 1\n127:             continue\n128:         if key is not None:\n129:             opened[key] = service\n130:         merged.append(service)\n131: \n132:     for service in merged:\n133:         if not isinstance(service, dict):\n134:             continue\n135:         methods, count = _deduplicate_named(service.get(\"methods\"))\n136:         service[\"methods\"] = methods\n137:         removed += count\n138:     return merged, removed\n139: \n140: \n141: def _deduplicate_ports(ports):\n142:     if not isinstance(ports, dict):\n143:         return ports, 0\n144:     removed = 0\n145:     for repository in ports.get(\"repositories\") or []:\n146:         if not isinstance(repository, dict):\n147:             continue\n148:         methods, count = _deduplicate_named(repository.get(\"methods\"))\n149:         repository[\"methods\"] = methods\n150:         removed += count\n151:     for mapping in ports.get(\"entity_mappings\") or []:\n152:         if not isinstance(mapping, dict):\n153:             continue\n154:         indexes, count = _deduplicate_strings(mapping.get(\"indexes\"))\n155:         mapping[\"indexes\"] = indexes\n156:         removed += count\n157:     return ports, removed\n158: \n159: \n160: def _deduplicate_named(methods):\n161:     \"\"\"Remove items whose `name` repeats, keeping the first of each name.\n162: \n163:     Each surviving method also has its own duplicate parameter names removed:\n164:     the same free-text repeat can occur one level down.\n165:     \"\"\"\n166:     if not isinstance(methods, list):\n167:         return methods, 0\n168: \n169:     kept = []\n170:     seen = set()\n171:     removed = 0\n172:     for method in methods:\n173:         if not isinstance(method, dict):\n174:             kept.append(method)\n175:             continue\n176:         name = method.get(\"name\")\n177:         if isinstance(name, str):\n178:             key = name.strip().lower()\n179:             if key in seen:\n180:                 removed += 1\n181:                 continue\n182:             seen.add(key)\n183:         params, count = _deduplicate_params(method.get(\"params\"))\n184:         method[\"params\"] = params\n185:         removed += count\n186:         kept.append(method)\n187:     return kept, removed\n188: \n189: \n190: def _deduplicate_params(params):\n191:     if not isinstance(params, list):\n192:         return params, 0\n193:     kept = []\n194:     seen = set()\n195:     removed = 0\n196:     for param in params:\n197:         if not isinstance(param, dict):\n198:             kept.append(param)\n199:             continue\n200:         name = param.get(\"name\")\n201:         if isinstance(name, str):\n202:             key = name.strip().lower()\n203:             if key in seen:\n204:                 removed += 1\n205:                 continue\n206:             seen.add(key)\n207:         kept.append(param)\n208:     return kept, removed\n209: \n210: \n211: def _deduplicate_strings(values):\n212:     if not isinstance(values, list):\n213:         return values, 0\n214:     kept = []\n215:     seen = set()\n216:     removed = 0\n217:     for value in values:\n218:         if isinstance(value, str):\n219:             key = value.strip().lower()\n220:             if key in seen:\n221:                 removed += 1\n222:                 continue\n223:             seen.add(key)\n224:         kept.append(value)\n225:     return kept, removed"
              }
