            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/extraction/repairs.py, lines 389-448\n389: def repair_placeholder_subcommands(components, log):\n390:     \"\"\"Drop a subcommand whose name is a placeholder.\n391: \n392:     A subcommand named `none` states that the command takes no subcommand —\n393:     library's bare `` `library overdue` `` line came back as command `overdue`\n394:     with subcommand `none`, which no method can serve and no CLI framework can\n395:     route. The grammar leaves subcommand names free text, so presence of a\n396:     placeholder cannot be unrepresentable; it is removed here, leaving the\n397:     command with no subcommands, which is what the requirements describe. Only\n398:     the placeholder entries go: real siblings are untouched, and every removal\n399:     is logged.\n400:     \"\"\"\n401:     if not isinstance(components, dict):\n402:         return components\n403:     facade = components.get(\"facade\")\n404:     if not isinstance(facade, dict):\n405:         return components\n406:     invocation = facade.get(\"invocation\")\n407:     if not isinstance(invocation, dict):\n408:         return components\n409:     commands = invocation.get(\"commands\")\n410:     if not isinstance(commands, list):\n411:         return components\n412:     for command in commands:\n413:         if not isinstance(command, dict):\n414:             continue\n415:         subcommands = command.get(\"subcommands\")\n416:         if not isinstance(subcommands, list):\n417:             continue\n418:         kept = [\n419:             sub for sub in subcommands\n420:             if not (isinstance(sub, dict) and _is_placeholder_name(sub.get(\"name\")))\n421:         ]\n422:         removed = len(subcommands) - len(kept)\n423:         if removed:\n424:             if log is not None:\n425:                 log.write(\n426:                     f\"[ok] step components: command '{command.get('name')}' had \"\n427:          