                "type": "text",
                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/extraction/repairs.py, lines 1-50\n1: \"\"\"The two contradictions a grammar cannot express, removed deterministically.\n2: \n3: The project's rule is consistency *by construction*: a value that must not exist\n4: is made unrepresentable in the GBNF, and a prompt sentence is the second line of\n5: defence, not the first. Three defects stay outside both, because they are global\n6: properties of the document rather than the shape of any one field:\n7: \n8: - **Two declared errors for one missing thing.** `CategoryNotFoundError` and\n9:   `MissingCategoryError` are the same failure; whether two names mean one thing is\n10:   a comparison *between* entries, and GBNF cannot express \"distinct subjects over\n11:   an unbounded alphabet\" any more than it can express \"distinct method names\"\n12:   (§9.7). The prompt says one name per failure and the model wrote two.\n13: - **A create that reports a not-found of what it creates.** `create_product`\n14:   raising `ProductNotFoundError` needs the method's *verb* and its *noun* to be\n15:   compared against the error's noun; the contract grammar leaves both names free,\n16:   so it cannot.\n17: - **A transform that does not fit the field's name.** `DECIMAL_TO_CENTS` on\n18:   `copies` needs the field's *name* and its *transform* to agree on a kind of\n19:   value; the adapter grammar closes `transform` to an enum and `field_name` to\n20:   free text, so the pair is not a regular property either.\n21: - **A field sent past its own parameter.** `category_id` mapped into `data`\n22:   while the method declares a `category_id` needs the field's *name* and the\n23:   method's *parameter list* to be compared; neither the prompt block nor the\n24:   grammar relates the two, so it cannot.\n25: \n26: This is the same move as `dedupe.py` (§9.7): a *removal* of something that\n27: contradicts the rest of the document, never the invention or rewriting of a\n28: value. Every decision is logged, and the predicates are imported from\n29: `kernel.consistency` — the checker is the single definition of each\n30: contradiction, so a repair and the rule that reports it can never disagree. Run\n31: after every step that produces the documents it touches, and before writing.\n32: \"\"\"\n33: \n34: import re\n35: \n36: from kernel.consistency import checks_adapters, checks_errors\n37: from kernel.consistency import checks_surface as surface_checks\n38: from kernel.consistency.methods import PLACEHOLDER_VALUES, param_names\n39: from kernel.consistency.naming import normalize\n40: from kernel.codegen import bind_field, is_entity_type, option_dest\n41: \n42: \n43: def repair_errors(errors, services, log):\n44:     \"\"\"Remove the two error-registry contradictions; return `(errors, services)`.\n45: \n46:     The order matters: duplicates are resolved (and their `raises` references\n47:     redirected) *before* the create/not-found raises are dropped, so a reference\n48:     that becomes contradictory only after a redirect is still caught.\n49: \n50:     Doing nothing to a document that cannot hold the defect is deliberate: a\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 51]"
