          "type": "text",
          "text": "Done — both points handled, 505 tests green.\n\n**1. Clearer end-of-run message — implemented.**\nYour command stays the same, but `--chat` now always ends with:\n```\n==== SUMMARY ====\nblockers: N, open tie(s): M\nGENERATABLE: YES — `generator.py` can run on this output\n```\nor `GENERATABLE: NO` with the exact blocker list (rule + message) and any ties still needing a human. Detail stays in `run.log`; the verdict is the only line that answers the question. Code: `report_verdict()` in `extract_arch.py`, called on every `chat_loop` exit path.\n\nI did not suppress the per-step lines yet — say the word if you want a `--quiet` mode that keeps detail file-only.\n\n**2. The blocker — root cause + fix implemented, needs one rerun to apply.**\nCause: the model emits both `member` + subcommand `history` (correct, carries `--member-id`) and a flat `member_history` with no subcommands. The flat form matches no method (`checks_surface.py:292`), so the probe reports `[unbacked_command] 'member_history member_history'` and the generator refuses.\n\nFix: `repair_flat_command_duplicates()` in `kernel/extraction/repairs.py` — drops a flat `a_b` only when the `a`+`b` pair exists, keeping the form with the subcommand. Grounded removal, no invention. Wired into `pipeline.py:_step_components` for first attempt + retry. Verified on a copy of your current docs: 1 blocker → 0 (1 note-level risk remains, non-blocking).\n\nTo apply it to `out/library` (code fix doesn't rewrite your docs):\n```\nMODEL=../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf\ncaffeinate -s -i python3 extract_arch.py --model \"$MODEL\" --output out/library --from-step components\n```\nThen `python3 generator.py out/library` should proceed instead of refusing.",
