                "text": "Read file /Users/gillesstenger/Documents/esus/kernel/extraction/pipeline.py, lines 1-75\n1: \"\"\"The extraction steps, run in order and chained.\n2: \n3: Each step receives the names its predecessors actually produced, both in the\n4: prompt (as an authoritative list) and in its grammar (as the only writable\n5: strings). Steps whose predecessor produced nothing usable fall back to the\n6: unconstrained grammar and say so in the log, so a degraded run is visible\n7: rather than silent.\n8: \"\"\"\n9: \n10: import json\n11: import re\n12: import sys\n13: \n14: from kernel.consistency.checks_crud import check_crud_coverage\n15: from kernel.consistency.checks_surface import check_flag_coverage, check_surface_coverage\n16: from kernel.consistency.report import Report\n17: from kernel.extraction import (\n18:     classification,\n19:     command_lines,\n20:     dedupe,\n21:     grammar_builders,\n22:     grammar_check,\n23:     grammar_open,\n24:     grammar_persistence,\n25:     interfaces,\n26:     prompts,\n27:     repairs,\n28:     return_types,\n29:     runner,\n30:     vocabulary,\n31: )\n32: \n33: # Greedy decoding plus a fixed seed: the same prompt yields the same document\n34: # (modulo GPU arithmetic), so a healed rerun proves the fix rather than luck.\n35: # Reproducibility is diagnostic, not corrective — but the first attempt is the\n36: # baseline everything is judged against, so it stays cold and reproducible.\n37: TEMPERATURE = 0.0\n38: SEED = 20261012\n39: \n40: # A second attempt at a higher temperature, used when a step returns something\n41: # JSON rejects — and, deliberately, for coverage retries too. Measured\n42: # 2026-10-13: three temp-0 library runs came back token-identical, and a cold\n43: # coverage retry re-asked and re-omitted the same two commands. A retry that\n44: # cannot differ cannot heal; the first attempt stays reproducible, the retry\n45: # explores once, and the probe judges the result either way.\n46: RET