          "text": "You were right about the param — and it was already set. `runner.py:108` passes `verbose=False` to `Llama()`, but that only gates the wrapper's Python logs (via `set_verbose`). The `ggml_metal_*` compile banners and loader lines are written by the C layer straight to the file descriptors, bypassing it entirely — which is why they still show.\n\nFix, active only under `--quiet`: `load_model()` now wraps the `Llama(...)` construction in the binding's own fd-level redirect (`llama_cpp._utils.suppress_stdout_stderr`, the same helper the wrapper uses for backend init), with a `nullcontext` fallback for very old bindings. Generation calls need no wrapping — they're silent; failures still raise as exceptions.\n\nCovered by 2 new tests in `tests/test_quiet.py` (quiet suppresses + still passes `verbose=False`; loud path constructs unwrapped). Full suite: 513 green.\n\nSame manual command as before — `--quiet` should now also swallow the metal banners:\n```\nMODEL=../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf\ncaffeinate -s -i python3 extract_arch.py --model \"$MODEL\" --output out/library --requirements prompts/prompt_library_system.txt --chat --quiet\n```",
