          "type": "text",
          "text": "Fixed and verified for real this time — 2 lines out for the extractor load, 1 for the classifier-style load, down from ~50.\n\nRoot cause, found by bisection: the banners never came from the model load. They come from `resolve_gpu_layers()` → `llama_supports_gpu_offload()`, which initializes the Metal backend (device discovery + shader compile) just to answer \"is offload supported\" — and `load_model` called it *outside* my redirect, twice (once for the `[model] ... on Metal` label, once for the constructor kwarg). My first fix wrapped only the constructor, so the probe kept shouting. Now the probe and the construction both run inside the fd redirect under `--quiet` (loud path unchanged).\n\nA test pins the ordering: `suppress-enter` → `probe` → `Llama` → `exit` (`tests/test_quiet.py`). Suite: 513 green.\n\nYour command should now be quiet end to end:\n```\nMODEL=../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf\ncaffeinate -s -i python3 extract_arch.py --model \"$MODEL\" --output out/library --requirements prompts/prompt_library_system.txt --chat --quiet\n```",
