          "type": "text",
          "text": "Evidence first: it just generated — 11 methods implemented, 3 aggregate stubs — but the 7 files are the standard argparse set, `cli.py` included. So:\n\n1. **No, the generator doesn't know pyimgui.** It honors the facade declaration nowhere; the docstring states argparse-always as a deliberate deferral (same as the click port). Your `gui/pyimgui` declaration sits unused in `components.json`, and the \"adapter fields with no CLI flag\" flood is the symptom: 26 fields with no flags because a GUI has no flags.\n2. **Should extraction specify forms/events? Eventually, but it's not the next step.** Split it:\n   * *Generic CRUD GUI* needs no new spec — models + crud_services + adapters already describe it (one table per entity, add/edit/delete wired to the services). The requirements' bespoke screens (assign bottles to Rack A/Shelf 3, over-capacity warnings) are what want specified forms/events.\n   * *Specified forms/events* means a new extraction surface (views bound to adapters) — grammar work, checker rules, generator binding. Real design, real cost.\n\nMy recommendation: a generic `gui.py` pyimgui emitter now (bounded, no extraction change, announced as generic), specified views later if the generic one proves insufficient. Want me to build the generic emitter?",
