        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Not an installation problem — a macOS context problem, fixed in the emitter and regenerated.\n\nCause: macOS gives GLFW a legacy OpenGL context by default; pyimgui's stock `GlfwRenderer` compiles core-profile shaders against it, and the first GL call (`glGetUniformLocation`) fails with 1282. The documented fix (same as pyimgui's own `example_glfw.py`) is requesting OpenGL 3.2 forward-compatible core profile *before* creating the window — `gui.py` now does that, with the reason in a comment.\n\nRegenerated in place — rerun:\n```\npython3.12 out/gui/generated/gui.py\n```\n\nCaveat, stated plainly: I can't execute the window loop here (no display), so this last mile is verified by you, not me. If it opens with three entity windows, we're done; if macOS throws anything else, paste the traceback — we're now past generated-code bugs and into platform territory.",
          "state": {
            "itemId": "msg_01a13ab608c876a6bd415a42520c442b"
          }
        }
      ],
