      "summary": "## Objective\n- Drive an LLM architecture-extraction pipeline (requirements → JSON docs → Python code) to zero generator blockers, then meter mechanical coverage; currently building the human-in-the-loop slot review (aggregate/threshold patterns) while guards with business logic wait for a follow-up discussion.\n\n## Requirements\n- JSON per prompt must be consistent and compliant with the prompt; ignore old md reports.\n- Use Ministral from `../models`; `caffeinate` for long Mac runs.\n- `prompts/*.txt` frozen (triage copies in `backup/prompts_triage/`); temp=0, seed 20261012.\n- No catalog additions (uncovered patterns → documented stubs / LLM pass); generator must refuse blocked docs, never invent silently.\n- Human answers persist (`decisions.json`, `field_aliases.json`, `surface_decisions.json`), prompt-hash stamped, re-applied on reruns.\n- `--quiet` mode: plan + per-step progress lines + verdict on terminal; full detail in `run.log`.\n- GUI: `generator.py` takes `--gui-tech` param, dispatches on declared technology; generic emitter (no bespoke screens).\n- Every mechanical codegen step must be finished; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`; meter mechanical coverage.\n- Windows/Linux/macOS portability of generated `gui.py`.\n- Slot review scope now (\"build it\"), guards with business logic discussed after.\n\n## Decisions\n- Same prompt + temp 0 + seed `20261012` reproduces byte-near-identical output.\n- `--quiet` shows step plan, one progress line per step, token-timing, review questions, `==== SUMMARY ====` with `GENERATABLE: YES/NO`; resumes don't re-print the plan.\n- llama.cpp native noise suppressed under `--quiet` via fd-level `suppress_stdout_stderr` wrapping both the offload probe and model construction.\n- Degenerate case (0 blockers, clean-but-empty docs) → LLM fallback writes one `generated/app.py` from `requirements.txt` (only with `--model`; exit 2 without); compile gate refuses unparseable output.\n- GUI generic pyimgui 