tion spec + the target method's params + return shape → from ctx docs.\n- usage: mutable dict collecting {action: [dests]} for argv augmentation.\n\nAlternate candidate computation:\n```python\ndef _alternate_actions(ctx, base_action, dests, actions):\n    base = actions.get(base_action) or {}\n    service = base.get(\"target_service\")\n    candidates = []\n    for name in sorted(actions):\n        spec = actions[name]\n        if name == base_action or spec.get(\"target_service\") != service:\n            continue\n        fields = [f for f in spec.get(\"input_fields\") or [] if isinstance(f, dict) and f.get(\"field_name\")]\n        if not fields:\n            continue  # paramless actions are route territory, not value filters\n        binds = []\n        ok = True\n        for field in fields:\n            dest = codegen.bind_field(dests, field[\"field_name\"])\n            if dest is None or dest in binds:\n                ok = False\n                break\n            binds.append(dest)\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n        # internal consistency: every field names a parameter of its own target method\n        params = _method_params(ctx, spec.get(\"target_service\"), spec.get(\"target_method\"))\n        if params is None:  # method not found → cannot verify\n            continue\n        if not all(field[\"field_name\"] in params for field in fields):  # flat equality?\n            continue\n        shape = _method_return(ctx, ...)\n        if shape not in (\"collection\", \"entity\"):\n            continue\n        candidates.append((name, list(zip([f[\"field_name\"] for f in fields], binds))))\n    return candidates\n```\nHmm — field name vs param: \"category_id\" == \"category_id\" exact ✓; month ✓. Use exact (after normalize? plain equality — docs are consistent). Wait: what about transforms like field_name \"author_id\" vs param \"author_id\" ✓. Keep exact string equality (conservative).\n\n_method_params: find in ctx[\"repositories\"] (en