efactor.**\n\nActually — to minimize churn: keep _emit_options as-is but extend the destinations append to include type: currently appends `(dest, flags[0])`. The plan says destinations (dest, flag, kind). Inside _emit_options I have `otype`. So append `(dest, flags[0], otype == \"bool\")`? Hmm — kind: bool → \"truthy\", else \"value\". Let me append `(dest, flags[0], \"truthy\" if otype == \"bool\" else \"value\")`.\n\nBut I ALSO need _plan_options for phase 0 (destinations WITHOUT rendering/emitting)... Wait — do I? Phase 0 needs the destinations per leaf BEFORE BINDINGS emission; the parser rendering happens later. If _emit_options both plans and renders, I can't call it early (line order in the emitted file). So yes, refactor: \n\n```python\ndef _option_plans(options, stats):\n    \"\"\"Emitted `(dest, flags, type)` per declared option — one planning pass\n    so the parser lines and the binding choices read the same skips.\"\"\"\n    plans = []\n    seen = set()\n    taken = {\"-h\", \"--help\"}\n    for option in options or []:\n        if not isinstance(option, dict):\n            continue\n        raw = ...\n        ... (same skip logic, but append plan dict)\n        plans.append({\"raw\": raw, \"dest\": dest, \"flags\": flags, \"type\": otype})  # needed fields for rendering: flags, dest, otype, required, default\n    return plans\n```\nThe render needs: flags, otype, required, default, dest. So plan carries them all: {\"flags\": flags, \"otype\": otype, \"required\": required, \"default\": default, \"dest\": dest}.\n\n```python\ndef _render_plan(indent, parser_var, plan):\n    parts = [repr(flag) for flag in plan[\"flags\"]]\n    otype = plan[\"otype\"]; required = plan[\"required\"]; default = plan[\"default\"]\n    ... same as now ...\n    parts.append(f\"dest={plan['dest']!r}\")\n    return f\"{indent}{parser_var}.add_argument({', '.join(parts)})\"\n\n\ndef _emit_options(indent, parser_var, options, stats, destinations=None):\n    lines = []\n    for p