      "summary": "## Objective\n- Drive the LLM architecture-extraction pipeline (prompts → JSON docs → runnable Python) to zero generator blockers with human-in-the-loop reviews, and make \"mechanical\" mean \"actually works\" — audit and fix emitted bodies and CLI surfaces that trap, ignore flags, or read the wrong entity.\n\n## Requirements\n- JSON per prompt must be consistent and compliant with the prompt; ignore old md reports.\n- Use Ministral from `../models`; `caffeinate` for long Mac runs.\n- `prompts/*.txt` frozen (triage copies in `backup/prompts_triage/`); temp=0, seed 20261012.\n- No catalog additions (uncovered patterns → documented stubs / LLM pass); generator must refuse blocked docs, never invent silently.\n- Human answers persist (`decisions.json`, `field_aliases.json`, `surface_decisions.json`, `method_slots.json`), prompt-hash stamped, re-applied on reruns.\n- `--quiet` mode: plan + per-step progress + verdict on terminal; full detail in `run.log`.\n- GUI: `generator.py --gui-tech` dispatches on declared technology to the generic emitter.\n- Every mechanical codegen step must be finished; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`; meter mechanical coverage.\n- Generated `gui.py` must stay portable across Windows/Linux/macOS.\n\n## Decisions\n- FILTER_CRITERION built (approved): parameterless list method whose filter-ish pattern stubs gets one finite question — field (boolean → True/False; string → only invariant-documented values via `must be one of [...]`) and value; unverifiable literal refuses to stub. Answers recorded: `find_active_members` is_active=True, `find_inactive_members` is_active=False, `get_active_loans` status='active' (user confirmed literal reading over \"not returned\").\n- Dead CLI flags: kept in the emitted surface (docs' surface), reported as generation-time findings (`dead option: ... — no adapter field reads it`), never silently dropped.\n- User approved building option-selected actions: recorded routes (kind:\"route\" in