          pass\n            def delete_product(self, id=None):\n                deleted.append(id)\n            def read_one_product(self, id=None):\n                return f\"read:{id}\"\n\n        code, out = self.run_cli(text, {\"ProductRepository\": ProductRepository},\n                                 [\"product\", \"remove\", \"-id\", \"7\"])\n        self.assertEqual(code, 0)\n        self.assertEqual(deleted, [7])\n        self.assertNotIn(\"read:7\", out)\n```\nNote: `run_cli` default models (\"Member\",\"Budget\",\"Product\") — the emitted MODELS = ['Product'] anyway ✓ fine.\n\nCareful about `next(l for l in ...)` if line wraps — BINDINGS lines are single lines even long ✓.\n\nAlso there may be additional BINDINGS lines in the text containing \"('product', 'remove')\" — only one ✓.\n\nNow, will `('product','remove')` bind via COMMAND_VERB_STEMS? real library `product remove` bound to a remove/delete action ✓. In my mini ctx: action name remove_product; verb stem \"remove\" ✓ likely.\n\nOne consideration for member_ctx: will bind_commands pick list_members for ('member','list')? Real library did ✓.\n\nNow test_surface.py additions:\n\n```python\ndef route_docs(directory, requirements=\"Run `member list [--active-only]`.\"):\n    \"\"\"A library-like surface with a stranded flag on a paramless read.\"\"\"\n    path = Path(directory)\n    components = {\"facade\": {\"type\": \"cli\", \"technology\": \"argparse\",\n                             \"invocation\": {\"commands\": [\n                                 {\"name\": \"member\", \"options\": [], \"subcommands\": [\n                                     {\"name\": \"list\", \"options\": [\n                                         {\"name\": \"-active-only\", \"short\": \"-a\",\n                                          \"type\": \"bool\", \"required\": False,\n                                          \"default\": None}]}]}]}}}\n    ...\n```\nWait the existing `writes()` writes `{\"components\": components(cmds)}` where components() returns the facade dict — payload key \"components\" → facade at payload[\"components\"][\"facade\"] ✓ I'll follow.\n\nLet me write a helper mirroring writes() but with real adapters/ports/model/matches:\n\n```python\ndef route_output(directory, routes=(), candidates_decided=True):\n    path = Path(directory)\n    (path / \"requirements.txt\").write_text(\n        \"Run `member list [--active-only]`.\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (path / \"components.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"components\": components([\n        {\"name\": \"member\", \"options\": [], \"subcommands\": [\n            {\"name\": \"list\", \"options\": [\n                {\"name\": \"-active-only\", \"short\": \"-a\", \"type\": \"bool\",\n                 \"required\": False, \"default\": None}]}]}])}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (path / \"data_models.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"data_models\": [\n        {\"name\": \"Member\", \"fields\": [\n            {\"name\": \"id\", \"type\": \"int\", \"primary_key\": True},\n            {\"name\": \"is_active\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}]}]}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (path / \"interaction_adapters.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"interaction_adapters\": [\n        {\"action_name\": \"list_members\", \"target_service\": \"MemberRepository\",\n         \"target_method\": \"read_all_members\", \"input_fields\": []}]}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (path / \"persistence_ports.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"persistence_ports\": {\n        \"repositories\": [\n            {\"entity\": \"Member\", \"interface_name\": \"MemberRepository\", \"methods\": [\n                {\"name\": \"read_all_members\", \"params\": [],\n                 \"return_type\": \"List[Member]\"},\n                {\"name\": \"find_active_members\", \"params\": [],\n                 \"return_type\": \"List[Member]\"},\n                {\"name\": \"find_members_by_name\",\n                 \"params\": [{\"name\": \"name\", \"type\": \"str\"}],\n                 \"return_type\": \"List[Member]\"}]}],\n        \"entity_mappings\": [{\"entity\": \"Member\", \"table\": \"members\",\n                             \"primary_key\": \"id\", \"indexes\": []}]}}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (path / \"pattern_matches.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"pattern_matches\": [\n        {\"source\": \"contract:MemberRepository.read_all_members\",\n         \"pattern_id\": \"READ_ALL\", \"decision\": \"decided\"},\n        {\"source\": \"contract:MemberRepository.find_active_members\",\n         \"pattern_id\": \"READ_ALL\", \"decision\": \"decided\"},\n        {\"source\": \"contract:MemberRepository.find_members_by_name\",\n         \"pattern_id\": \"READ_ALL\", \"decision\": \"decided\"}]}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for name in (\"service_contracts\", \"errors\", \"intentions\", \"invariants\"):\n        (path / f\"{name}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({name: []}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if routes:\n        (path / \"surface_decisions.json\").write_text(json.dumps(\n            {\"decisions\": list(routes)}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return str(path)\n```\n\nHmm — but wait: find_members_by_name with READ_ALL decided → plan_method: crud = filter (name starts with find) with params → `payload in MECHANICAL_PATTERNS and crud is not None` → \"crud:filter\" usable — but it's excluded by the params check in _route_candidates ✓ so it won't show; that's part of the test assertion (only paramless candidates listed).\n\nTests:\n```python\nclass RouteCollectTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_stranded_flag_offers_parameterless_reads(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n            out = route_output(directory)\n            questions, _ = collect_routes(out)\n            self.assertEqual(len(questions), 1)\n            question = questions[0]\n            self.assertEqual((question[\"command\"], question[\"subcommand\"],\n                              question[\"flag\"]), (\"member\", \"list\", \"active_only\"))\n            self.assertEqual(question[\"candidates\"],\n                             [(\"MemberRepository\", \"find_active_members\")])\n\n    def test_recording_a_route_closes_the_question(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n            out = route_output(directory)\n            run_review(out, input_fn=lambda _: \"1\", out_fn=lambda _: None)\n            self.assertEqual(collect_routes(out)[0], [])\n            records = json.loads((Path(out) / generator.SURFACE_DECISIONS_NAME).read_text())[\"decisions\"]\n            self.assertEqual(records[0][\"kind\"], \"route\")\n            self.assertEqual(records[0][\"method\"], \"find_active_members\")\n```\nWait — for `run_review` with route questions, is the numbering/flow okay with input \"1\"? ask_route: answer \"1\" → candidates[0] ✓.\n\nBut — careful: `run_review` reads components.json and applies; fine.\n\nAnd after recording, collect_routes should return no questions: the flag is still dead per _leaf_scan? No — the route record makes _leaf_choices add the route choice consuming the flag → dead empty → no question ✓. Also `decided` check ✓. \n\nAnother test: route record with a candidate whose method doesn't exist → ignored (generator side `_service_method` None → skip; question reopened?) — the `decided` set would exclude it from questions though (record exists) — hmm: collect_routes' `decided` check would SKIP the question even though the record is bogus (service/method invalid). Should `decided` only count records that actually apply? The generator drops nothing (it keeps the record but doesn't wire it); the review wouldn't re-ask → slight inconsistency. Improve: only treat records as decided when their leaf/flag would actually be consumed... Simpler: when building `decided`, validate the record resolves: service/method exist. But collect_routes doesn't have leaves' bound... it does! Let me refine: in collect_routes, for decided routes, check `generator._service_method(ctx, record[\"service\"], r