allback (no explicit quiet).\n\nNow the fill driver:\n\n```python\ndef fill_stubs(files, ctx, stats, model_path):\n    \"\"\"Ask the model for every stub body the emitter refused; return count.\n\n    Runs only when `--model` is passed. Each module is filled stub by stub;\n    a body that does not compile is reverted to its stub and reported —\n    nothing unverified is ever written. The model is loaded once for the\n    whole run.\n    \"\"\"\n    targets = [name for name in (\"repositories.py\", \"services.py\")\n               if name in files]\n    todo = []\n    for name in targets:\n        for span in find_stub_spans(files[name]):\n            todo.append((name, span))\n    if not todo:\n        return 0\n    requirements = load_requirements(...)  # need out_dir! pass ctx? \n```\nHmm — requirements: `load_requirements(out_dir)`. main has args.out_dir; pass requirements text into fill_stubs from main (main can read it) or pass out_dir. generate_fallback reads load_requirements(out_dir) itself; fill_stubs can take out_dir too... but main already has args.out_dir. Signature: `fill_stubs(files, ctx, stats, model_path, requirements_text)`.\n\nOrder: repositories first then services — because services may call repo methods; and for services the reference list should reflect the FILLED repos. So: iterate file by file: fill repositories.py fully, then compute references from the updated repositories.py text for services.py.\n\nReferences for services: distill repo class methods from the CURRENT repositories.py text:\n```python\ndef _method_signatures(text):\n    \"\"\"`Class.method(signature) -> returns` lines for the prompt's reference.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    cls = None\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        m = re.match(r\"^class (\\w+)\", line)\n        if m: cls = m.group(1)\n        m = re.match(r\"^    def (\\w+\\(.*\\) -> .*):$\", line)\n        if m and cls: out.append(f\"{cls}.{m.group(1)}\")\n    return out\n```\nCareful with def lines ending with \