      "summary": "## Objective\n- Drive the LLM architecture-extraction pipeline (prompts → JSON docs → runnable Python) to zero generator blockers with human-in-the-loop reviews, and make \"mechanical\" mean \"actually works\" — audit and fix emitted bodies and CLI surfaces that trap, ignore flags, or read the wrong entity. Latest block: an LLM pass inside the generator that fills refused stubs.\n\n## Requirements\n- JSON per prompt must be consistent and compliant with the prompt; ignore old md reports.\n- Use Ministral from `../models`; `caffeinate` for long Mac runs; temp=0, seed 20261012.\n- `prompts/*.txt` frozen (triage copies in `backup/prompts_triage/`).\n- No catalog additions (uncovered patterns → documented stubs / LLM pass); generator must refuse blocked docs, never invent silently.\n- Human answers persist (`decisions.json`, `field_aliases.json`, `surface_decisions.json`, `method_slots.json`), prompt-hash stamped, re-applied on reruns.\n- `--quiet` mode (extract side): plan + per-step progress + verdict on terminal; full detail in `run.log`.\n- GUI: `generator.py --gui-tech` dispatches on declared technology to the generic emitter.\n- Every mechanical codegen step must be finished; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`; meter mechanical coverage.\n- Generated `gui.py` must stay portable across Windows/Linux/macOS.\n- LLM pass placement (user, latest): add it to `generator.py`, not `extract_arch.py`; \"llm generate what is left unimplemented\"; \"for now we check manually the resulting code\" (no review/persistence machinery yet).\n\n## Decisions\n- FILTER_CRITERION (approved): parameterless filter-ish stubs get one finite question (field + value; string values only from invariant-documented vocabulary). Recorded: `find_active_members` is_active=True, `find_inactive_members` is_active=False, `get_active_loans` status='active'.\n- Dead CLI flags kept in the emitted surface, reported as generation-time findings (`dead option: ... — no adapter field re