          "type": "text",
          "text": "Found and fixed — the bug was mine, and it explains 5/5 identical rejections.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`extract_code()` ends with `.strip()` (right for whole programs, which is why `app.py` was fine). Applied to a **method body**, it strips the leading indentation of the **first line only** — every following line keeps its own. The min-indent dedent then computed 0, the body was re-indented, and the first line came out shallower than the rest → `compile()` refused with \"unexpected indent\". The model was answering in the module's own style (4- or 8-space base), which is exactly what triggered it; my tests had only ever exercised zero-indent answers, the one case that survived. The user-visible proof: `budget` — no wait, proof in my matrix: \"body at 4/8 spaces\" failed, \"body at 0\" passed.\n\n## Fix (commit `ab959a7`)\n\n- `extract_code(text, keep_indent=True)` for the fill path: the answer's indentation is preserved, so `_clean_body` dedents correctly.\n- `_clean_body` also drops an echoed `def` line **and** an echoed docstring (single- or multi-line) — models often return the whole method.\n- Every raw answer is now dumped to `out/<run>/llm_stub_answers.json` (label, status, note, raw text), so a refusal can be read instead of guessed at.\n\n## Verified without any model (as requested)\n\n- Answer formats 4-space / 8-space / fenced / whole-method / prose+fences: all assembled and compiled **OK** (all failed before). Only genuinely inconsistent indentation still refuses, with a note.\n- Mocked end-to-end on the real `out/library` modules with indented canned answers: **5/5 written**, both modules compile, docstrings tagged, dump written.\n- 615 non-LLM tests green; regenerations of `out/library` and `out/expenses` byte-identical.\n\n## To re-run (your call)\n\n```\npython3.12 generator.py out/library --model ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf\n```\n\nExpect `llm written:` lines for the five stubs, bodies tagged `[llm-written by … — review]`, and raw answers in `out/library/llm_stub_answers.json`. If the model still refuses one, the note plus the dump will say exactly why. The mocked pass tests, if you want them: `python3 -m unittest tests.test_generator.StubFillTests -v`.\n\nStill open from before: the `Budget.month` doc-vs-prompt inconsistency (prompt says `str \"YYYY-MM\"`; docs say date/ISO_DATE) awaits your decision on the extraction-side fix."
        }
