       return \"the model kept it unimplemented\"\n    unknown = sorted({name for name in re.findall(r\"self\\.(\\w+)\", text)\n                      if name not in module_names})\n    if unknown:\n        return f\"calls self.{unknown[0]}, which the module does not define\"\n    invented = sorted({name for name in re.findall(r\"self\\._store\\.(\\w+)\", text)\n                       if name not in store_names})\n    if invented:\n        return (f\"calls self._store.{invented[0]}, which the store does not \"\n                \"define\")\n    invented = sorted({name for name in re.findall(r\"\\bmodels\\.(\\w+)\", text)\n                       if name not in model_names})\n    if invented:\n        return f\"calls models.{invented[0]}, which models.py does not define\"\n    invented = sorted({name for name in re.findall(r\"\\berrors\\.(\\w+)\", text)\n                       if name not in error_names})\n    if invented:\n        return f\"calls errors.{invented[0]}, which errors.py does not define\"\n    return None\n```\n\nWait — careful with `self._store.all` etc: the `self\\.(\\w+)` regex on \"self._store.all\" matches `_store` ✓ in module_names (includes _store) — fine. And `\\bmodels\\.` on \"self._store.all\" no. On `models.Book` ✓.\n\nHmm — one subtlety: `models\\.(\\w+)` in a body line like `models.Book(**record)` → Book ✓ defined. What about attribute chains `models.Book.SOMETHING`? findall gets \"Book\" ✓.\n\nWhat about `from models import Book`? No `models.` → fine.\n\nEdit 4: fill_stubs — compute api + names:\n\nCurrent:\n```python\n    store_names = {match.group(1) for match in\n                   re.finditer(r\"^    def (\\w+)\", files.get(\"store.py\") or \"\",\n                               re.M)}\n    out(f\"llm: {todo} refused stub(s) — {model_name} writes them body by body\")\n```\n→\n```python\n    store_names = {match.group(1) for match in\n                   re.finditer(r\"^    def (\\w+)\", files.get(\"store.py\") or \"\",\n                               re.M)}\n    model_names = _class_names(files.get(\"models.py\") or \"\")\n    error_names = _class_names(files.get(\"errors.py\") or \"\")\n    api = _api_reference(files)\n    out(f\"llm: {todo} refused stub(s) — {model_name} writes them body by body\")\n```\n\nAnd the prompt call:\n```python\n            prompt = stub_prompt(requirements, text, info, references)\n```\n→\n```python\n            prompt = stub_prompt(requirements, text, info, references, api)\n```\n\nAnd the refusal call:\n```python\n            refusal = _body_refusal(body, _module_names(text), store_names)\n```\n→\n```python\n            refusal = _body_refusal(body, _module_names(text), store_names,\n                                    model_names, error_names)\n```\n\nEdit 5: fill_stubs docstring: \"may only touch `self.<name>` and `self._store.<name>` the module actually defines\" → \"may only touch `self.<name>`, `self._store.<name>`, `models.<name>` and `errors.<name>` the modules actually define\".\n\nAlso module docstring lines 44-49: \"...and it touches no `self.<name>` or store method that does not exist; ...\" → \"...and it names only `self.<name>`, store methods, `models.*` classes and `errors.*` classes the sibling modules define; ...\".\n\nLet me apply all edits now.",
