odule 'calendar' has no attribute 'localtime'` (latent: `book - 1` TypeError, `errors.BookUnavailableError`).\n- Harness fix `34753f6` (fake model classes); full non-LLM suite 615 green on this server; regenerations of `out/library` + `out/expenses` without `--model` remain byte-identical.\n- Commits on this server, all pulled by the Mac: `86ffecc` (routes/alternates), `34753f6` (harness), `ab959a7` (keep_indent + raw dump), `77e23cf` (compile note names offending line: `the body does not compile (… ; line N '<text>')`), `72275e1` (unpaired fence + calendar + regression test).\n\n### Active\n- Runtime quality of the five LLM bodies (4 of 5 fail when called; cause: prompt never showed `models` fields / `errors` names / record types — the model correctly used what it could see); awaiting user's go/no-go on the two proposed improvements.\n- `Budget.month` doc-vs-prompt inconsistency (finding, awaiting decision): prompt says `month (str like \"2024-01\")` and `get_monthly_report(month)` takes \"YYYY-MM\", but `out/expenses/data_models.json` types month `\"date\"` (+ `unique: true` vs prompt's `UNIQUE(category_id, month)`) and `interaction_adapters.json` has six `ISO_DATE` month inputs vs `create_budget` `DIRECT`; live: `budget list -category 1 -month 2026-10` → `Invalid isoformat string: '2026-10'`, with `2026-10-01` → 0 records.\n\n### Blocked\n- `out/60` and `out/inventory` runs are stale (Oct 12) and blocked on `[uncovered_field]` adapter blockers — re-run decision pending.\n- `__pycache__` untracking + `.gitignore` (87 tracked files churning) — awaiting user word.\n\n## Next Move\n1. On user's approval, implement the `stub_prompt` API section + `models.*`/`errors.*` guard, commit, and give them one rerun command (`git pull`; then `python3.12 generator.py out/library --model ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf`, then `out/expenses`).\n2. Await user decisions on the `Budget.month` extraction fix, `__pycache__` untracking, and re-running `out/60` + `out/inventory`.\n3. When asked, propose fixing the four broken bodies by hand or via a better-prompt rerun (bodies stay tagged in generated files until replaced).\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `generator.py`: LLM pass (`fill_stubs`, `stub_prompt`, `_clean_body`, `extract_code`), emission, `--model` help, module docstring.\n- `tests/test_generator.py`: `StubFillTests` (8 tests: written, whole-method, lone-fence, clean-body, compile-fail, invented names, nothing-to-fill, main+dump) — not run on this server; `MappingEmissionTests` harness fix.\n- `out/library/generated/repositories.py`, `services.py`: on this server still the mechanical version with stubs; the Mac's LLM-filled versions were never pushed back.\n- `out/library/llm_stub_answers.json`: on the Mac (overwritten each `--model` run); the five raw answers were pasted in conversation.\n- `/tmp/esus_llm_check/`: scratch replay of the five answers + seeded `smoke.db` used for the runtime review.\n- `kernel/extraction/runner.py`: `load_model`, `generate_free` (returns raw `choice[\"text\"]`, no trimming), `MAX_NEW_TOKENS=3584`.\n- `out/expenses/data_models.json`, `out/expenses/interaction_adapters.json`: the month inconsistency evidence.\n- `prompts/prompt_expenses.txt`: frozen prompt stating month is `str like \"2024-01\"`.\n- `../models/`: `Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf` (the one used), `…Q2_K_L.gguf`, Qwen3-4B.\n- `kernel/codegen_store_template.py`: store API (`add/get/all/update/delete/select`) used by the pass's guard.\n- `kernel/codegen.py`: `bind_field`, `plan_method`, `classify_crud`, `match_param`.\n- `review_surface.py`, `review_slots.py`: route/slot review owners (committed).\n- `meter_coverage.py`: mechanical coverage/stub ledger (LLM-filled still counted as stubs).\n- `out/library/surface_decisions.json`, `out/library/method_slots.json`: recorded human answers.\n\n## Important Context\n- This server is the Mac's git origin (`server.gillesstenger.fr:Documents/esus`); the Mac pulls here, runs the model there; its generated output is not pushed back. Server `python3` = 3.12; the Mac also runs `python3.12`.\n- The five real answers' shape: whole method (`def` + docstring) at 4-space base plus a lone closing ``` at indent 0; replaying them is deterministic (temp 0, seed 20261012, same model), which is why the scratch review reflects the Mac's run.\n- Body-runtime review details (exact errors) are in the chat; bodies are tagged `[llm-written by Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf — review]`; mechanical coverage stays 29/34 = 85%.\n- `fill_stubs` row contract: `(label, status, note)`, status `written`/`kept`; refusal notes: `the body does not compile (<msg>; line N '<line>')`, `calls self.X, …`, `calls self._store.X, …`, `the model kept it unimplemented`, `the model returned nothing`; model-load failure → single row `(N refused stub(s), kept, the model would not load (…))`.\n- Deliberately kept honest stubs: `book list -author` finding (\"action `list_books_by_author` mis-targets the availability filter\") and `expense report -yearly` finding (base has params → no alternates).\n- All commits are on this server's `main`; working tree clean except `__pycache__` churn; `out/library/generated` on this server does not yet contain the LLM bodies.\n- Command to run the mocked pass tests (Mac only): `python3 -m unittest tests.test_generator.StubFillTests -v`.",
      "recent": "[User]: yes\n\n[Assistant reasoning]: The user says \"yes\" — implement both improvements:\n1. stub_prompt gets an API section: models field lists per entity, errors class names, record-type note.\n2. A `models.*`/`errors.*` name guard in `_body_refusal`.\n\nThen hand them a rerun command. Let me plan carefully.\n\n### Current code structure\n\n`stub_prompt(requirements, module_text, info, references=(), budget=STUB_PROMPT_BUDGET)`:\n- builds instruction lines, references (repo signatures for services), requirements, module text fenced, then asks for the body.\n- Called from fill_stubs: `prompt = stub_prompt(requirements, text, info, references)` where `references` only set for services.py.\n\n`_body_refusal(body, module_names, store_names)`:\n- checks empty, NotImplementedError, unknown self.<name>, unknown self._store.<name>.\n\n### Design for improvement 1 (prompt API section)\n\nI need the models fields and errors names at prompt time. In `fill_stubs`, `files` includes \"models.py\" and \"errors.py\" (rendered files dict — check: render_program returns dict of all files incl. models.py, errors.py, store.py ✓ — yes, since _add_imports looks at... and store_names reads files[\"store.py\"]).\n\nSo build a compact API block:\n\n```\nAPI you may call:\n- Store records are dicts: `self._store.select(...)` / `.all(...)` yield\n  `{field: value}` — read with `record.get(\"title\")`.\n- Repository reads return dataclasses from models.py:\n  Book(id, title, isbn, published_year, available_copies, author_id)\n  Author(id, name, birth_year, biography)\n  Member(id, name, email, membership_date, is_active)\n  Loan(id, book_id, member_id, loan_date, due_date, return_date, status)\n  read their fields as attributes (`book.title`), never `.get(...)`.\n- errors.py defines: BookNotFoundError, AuthorNotFoundError, MemberNotFoundError, LoanNotFoundError, BookAlreadyExistsError, MemberAlreadyExistsError, InsufficientCopiesError, InvalidReturnDateError.\n- Importable