          "text": "Library review complete. The replay reproduced the Mac's run byte-for-byte (`5 of 5 written`), then the smoke pass told the real story:\n\n## Library body scoreboard (file-backed SQLite, as users run it)\n\n| body | verdict |\n|---|---|\n| `renew_membership` | ✅ toggles and persists (`True → False → True` verified) |\n| `LibraryService.search_books` | ✅ delegates correctly — but inherits its dependency's crash |\n| `BookRepository.search_books_by_title_author_isbn` | ❌ **any** non-title-matched book → `'int' object has no attribute 'lower'` (it lowercases `author_id`); `\"…\".search(query)` also doesn't exist; and the repo structurally *can't* search author **name** — it only sees `author_id` |\n| `return_book` | ❌ `Object of type datetime is not JSON serializable` — set `return_date = datetime.datetime.now()` (exactly what the model annotations promise!) but the store persists with `json.dumps` |\n| `borrow_book` | ❌ `'Book' object has no attribute 'copy'` — pydantic habit (`.copy(update=…)`) on a plain dataclass; also invents a 14-day due date the prompt never states (its guard paths are fine: 0 copies → clean `error: No available copies…`) |\n\n## Three findings with teeth\n\n1. **The date convention is a trap.** `out/library/generated/models.py` annotates `loan_date: datetime.datetime`, but `store._persist` does `json.dumps(record)` — so no body doing the *annotated* thing can ever save. Only adapter-supplied strings ever worked. Options: teach the store template to serialize date/datetime (one line in `kernel/codegen_store_template.py`), or declare an ISO-string convention in the prompt.\n2. **Mechanical defaults are dropped in extraction.** The prompt says `available_copies (default 1)` / `is_active (default True)`; `data_models.json` has no `default` key at all (`member add` in my smoke produced `\"is_active\": null`) — so `member list -active-only` and `find_active_members` never see CLI-created members. Extraction finding, like `Budget.month`.\n3. **Author-name search has no home.** `search_books(query)` is specced \"title/author/isbn\", but a repository can't join tables; only the *service* could via `AuthorRepository.read_all_authors()` + `find_books_by_author(id)`. Either accept title/ISBN in the repo layer, or the service does the composite.\n\n## Proposed next fixes (your go/no-go)\n\n- **A.** Store template: `json.dumps(..., default=…)` that ISO-formats dates — makes the models' annotations honest and fixes every program at once (with a regression test).\n- **B.** Prompt API section: print fields *with types* (`Book(id: int, title: str, …)`) and add one fact: models are plain dataclasses — mutate and pass back, no `.copy(update=…)`.\n- **C.** Your calls on: apply mechanical defaults (emitter side), where author search lives, and whether 14 days stays as an assumed policy.\n\nAnd paste the expenses dump when ready — `cat out/expenses/llm_stub_answers.json` — I'll run the same replay + smoke there."
