xport_to_csv ok (empty file presumably). detect → [].\n\n6. `budget list` works ✓ (month stored as string \"2026-10\" via my direct seed).\n\nSo I need to fix the driver AGAIN: use integer dollars for -amount (25, 45), `-monthly 2026-10-01` test (and expect NameError), `expense recurring` without detect. Let me also double-check what `-amount 25` stores: after the run, `expense list` should show amount_cents 2500 ✓ verify.\n\nAlso: the earlier `expense report` failing on ISO_DATE \"2026-10\" — with \"2026-10-01\" it will proceed to the body → NameError. Both worth showing.\n\nOne more consideration: the driver crashed earlier at export.csv read — now the flow continues. Rerun: but smoke.db already exists with seeded categories + budget + failed adds... rerunning the script would DUPLICATE categories (category add again → new ids 3,4?) — the script deletes/recreates the scratch copy but NOT smoke.db!! In drive.py (library) the scratch was rmtree'd entirely at the top; in drive_expenses.py I rmtree only SCRATCH/expenses; smoke.db lives in SCRATCH root (= /tmp/esus_llm_check2/smoke.db — hmm actually where did the library smoke.db live? In drive.py: GEN = SCRATCH/library/generated and DB path \"smoke.db\" relative to cwd=GEN → /tmp/esus_llm_check2/library/generated/smoke.db. In drive_expenses.py: cwd=GEN = SCRATCH/expenses/generated → smoke.db there. The expenses dir gets rmtree'd each run ✓ fresh ✓ good (scratch/expenses removed+recopied). ✓ So rerun = clean.\n\nLet me apply the edits: \n- amounts \"25.00\"→25, \"45.00\"→45 (as strings fine: \"-amount\", \"25\").\n- report: try BOTH: first `-monthly 2026-10` (expect Invalid isoformat) then `-monthly 2026-10-01 -yearly 2026` (expect NameError).\n- recurring: [\"expense\", \"recurring\"].\n- extra add also amount \"25\".\n\nEdit the bottom block again.",
