      "summary": "## Objective\n- Drive the LLM architecture-extraction pipeline (prompts → JSON docs → runnable Python) to zero generator blockers; latest stages: the LLM stub pass (`generator.py --model`) is filling 5/5 stubs in `out/library` and `out/expenses`, and the resulting bodies are being manually reviewed at runtime.\n\n## Requirements\n- `prompts/*.txt` frozen; JSON docs per prompt must be consistent and compliant with the prompt (triage copies in `backup/prompts_triage/`).\n- Ministral from `../models`; temp=0, seed 20261012; `caffeinate` for long Mac runs.\n- No catalog additions (no mechanical pattern → documented stub or LLM pass); generator must refuse blocked docs, never invent silently.\n- Human answers persist (`decisions.json`, `field_aliases.json`, `surface_decisions.json`, `method_slots.json`), prompt-hash stamped, re-applied on reruns.\n- `--quiet` on the extract side; GUI via `generator.py --gui-tech`; generated `gui.py` portable; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`; meter mechanical coverage.\n- LLM pass lives in `generator.py`; answers are checked manually, no review/persistence machinery.\n- Do not run the model on this server; tests that need the model are handed to the user as Mac commands.\n\n## Decisions\n- (Carried) FILTER_CRITERION answers for parameterless filter stubs; dead CLI flags kept and reported; option-selected actions choose routes → alternates → fallback (`86ffecc`); only a parameterless base method can be refined by flags; route review via `review_surface.py` records `kind:\"route\"`; `book list -author` and `expense report -yearly` stay findings.\n- LLM pass acceptance: module must `compile`, plus no invented `self.*`, `self._store.*`, `models.*`, `errors.*` names (guard extended in `2780ff6`); bodies tagged `[llm-written by <model> — review]` and still counted as stubs; every raw answer dumped to `<out>/llm_stub_answers.json`.\n- Stub prompt now carries an API section (model fields, error class names, record type