o available copies of this book`). Mechanical paths fine (`overdue`, `member history`, `member list -a`, `book list`, `member add`).\n- Root causes identified: (1) models annotate `loan_date: datetime.datetime` but `store._persist` does `json.dumps(record)` — the annotated thing can never be saved to a file DB; (2) prompt defaults (`available_copies` default 1, `is_active` default True) are absent from `data_models.json` → `member add` stores `is_active: null` → `find_active_members`/`member list -active-only` never see them; (3) author-name search has no home (repositories can't join; only the service could via `AuthorRepository.read_all_authors()` + `find_books_by_author(id)`).\n\n### Active\n- Proposed fixes awaiting user go/no-go: **A** store template `json.dumps(..., default=…)` ISO-formatting dates (`kernel/codegen_store_template.py` + regression test); **B** prompt API section prints fields with types (`Book(id: int, title: str, …)`) plus one fact line: models are plain dataclasses — mutate and pass back, no `.copy(update=…)`; **C** user calls on mechanical defaults, author-search location, 14-day policy.\n- Expenses run-3 review not started: `out/expenses/llm_stub_answers.json` not yet pasted; same replay + smoke to be done.\n- `run2_answers.json` (saved on the Mac) is an optional post-mortem for the falsely-refused `borrow_book` answer.\n- `Budget.month` doc-vs-prompt inconsistency (month typed `\"date\"` + `unique` in `out/expenses/data_models.json` vs prompt `str like \"2024-01\"`; live `budget list -category 1 -month 2026-10` → `Invalid isoformat string`) — awaiting decision.\n\n### Blocked\n- `out/60` and `out/inventory` runs are stale (Oct 12), blocked on `[uncovered_field]` adapter blockers — rerun decision pending.\n- `__pycache__` untracking + `.gitignore` (tracked files churning) — awaiting user word.\n\n## Next Move\n1. User pastes `out/expenses/llm_stub_answers.json`; replay it through `fill_stubs` in a scratch copy plus seeded smoke (same method