id for library). Correct output is not promised by the pass, only honest output.\n3. **More mechanical patterns** — ruled out (catalog additions).\n\nNote the pending expenses rerun won't settle this: A+B targeted the library classes, so with the same model its expected movement is small — worth doing for the ledger, not as a fix.\n\nMy recommendation: check `ls ../models` on the Mac. If there's a 7B+ instruct/code-capable model there, we run both programs with it (same command, different `--model`) and review — that's a clean A/B on model scale. If not, it's a \"download a bigger model or keep 3B + review\" decision. Either way the pipeline doesn't change; only the model argument does."
