      "summary": "## Objective\n- Drive the LLM architecture-extraction pipeline (prompts → JSON docs → runnable Python) to zero generator blockers; latest stage: deciding how to handle stub-filling quality (hand fixes vs. bigger model vs. static check + re-ask repair loop).\n\n## Requirements\n- `prompts/*.txt` frozen; JSON docs per prompt consistent/compliant (triage copies in `backup/prompts_triage/`).\n- Ministral from `../models`; temp=0, seed 20261012; `caffeinate` for long Mac runs; never run the model on this server — model steps are handed to the user as Mac commands.\n- No catalog additions; generator must refuse blocked docs, never invent silently; human answers persist (`decisions.json`, `field_aliases.json`, `surface_decisions.json`, `method_slots.json`), prompt-hash stamped, re-applied on reruns.\n- `--quiet` on extract side; GUI via `generator.py --gui-tech`; generated `gui.py` portable; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`.\n- LLM pass lives in `generator.py`; answers checked manually; no review/persistence machinery yet.\n- Generated output is never pushed back; Mac-local hand fixes are discarded if the program is regenerated (accepted).\n\n## Decisions\n- (Committed `d05fc5c`) Fix A: store normalizes dates to ISO at entry + `default=_iso` in `_persist`. Fix B: stub prompt lists model fields with types + facts \"plain dataclasses, no `copy(...)`\" and \"date fields hold ISO strings\".\n- (Approved) All three library hand fixes (repo search author join, return persists + guard, borrow returns loan; 14-day period, commented); patch script itself not committed.\n- (Established) Honest reading accepted: remaining stub-fill defects = LLM quality problem at 3B; pass is deterministic, so same model+prompt reproduces same bodies; levers are model upgrade or review — not more prompt wording.\n- (Established) A naive smoke repair loop is rejected as sole fix: it cannot catch silent defects (worst observed defect was silent). Verifier power is the constra