ous=None builds ✓.\n\n    Edge: if the previous answer contains the marker strings? No.\n\n3. Before handing over: validate the sweep script's logic on the server by dry-running it with a MOCKED model (no real generation): I can simulate: wrapper -> real calls replaced by mocks; run one fill; check the matrix prints, bare prompt transformation works, and scoring flows. But the script is Mac-side (uses real runner). For server validation, I can run the same script with a `--dry` env var that mocks runner.load_model/generate_free with the recorded answers (firsts) and echoes (repairs)? That tests the plumbing but not much else. Hmm — time. The script is mostly straightforward; the riskiest part is `generator.main([SWEEP])` mechanical-only path and the bare-prompt transform. Let me write it carefully and test those two pieces on the server (main mechanical run works — we know it does; bare transform — I can test in a small snippet on the server by building a repair prompt and transforming it).\n\n    Actually — I realize there's a subtlety with `generator.main([SWEEP])`: it may REFUSE if the copy contains a `generated/` directory with stale stuff? It regenerates; should be fine. Also main prints a lot; fine. Also main without --model: exit 0 if gate passes.\n\n    Another subtlety: fill_stubs(files, model_path, requirements, ...) needs `requirements` string — script: `generator.load_requirements(SWEEP)`.\n\n    Model path: pass as argv[1] or hardcode ../models/Ministral...? The user runs from repo root; pass via argv with default. `python3.12 temp_sweep.py ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf`. Hmm — where does the script live on the Mac? /tmp/temp_sweep.py — the user creates it (heredoc). Its sys.path.insert(0, \".\") then assumes cwd=repo root ✓ (they run from repo root).\n\n    How does the user get the script? I'll paste it as a `cat > /tmp/temp_sweep.py <<'PY' ... PY` block in my reply. Size ~120 lines — acceptable (the user has handled bigger).\n\n 