de.\n\nActually — one nuance: should the sweep results also inform Q2? The bare variant tests one prompt-shape change (not showing the refused answer). If bare@temp fixes search (the record.author case), that says the anchor made it worse, not the wording being insufficient. Point that out.\n\nAlso — I should be careful about one claim: \"at temp 0 + same seed, the repair call is the same call as the first ask *except the prompt differs*\". The repair prompt differs (complaints + previous shown) — so the echo is not strictly \"greedy re-completion of the first prompt\", it's greedy completion given a prompt that contains its own answer. That's the \"parrot by construction\" framing: the most probable continuation given \"here's your code + fix it\" is to reproduce the code. At temp 0 the model can't escape. Yes.\n\nOne more: seed variance. With seed fixed (+1) per cell and temp>0, each cell is still deterministic and reproducible — important for the \"accepted repair must be reviewable/deterministic\" ethos. State it.\n\nLength: keep the prose tight; the heredoc dominates. Let me write the reply.\n\nFormat of heredoc in reply: a fenced code block containing the cat command and script, then the run command in a separate block, or one block with both. I'll do:\n\n```bash\ncat > /tmp/temp_sweep.py <<'PY'\n<130 lines>\nPY\n\ncaffeinate python3.12 -u /tmp/temp_sweep.py ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf 2>&1 | tee /tmp/sweep_out.txt\n```\n\nThen \"paste /tmp/sweep_out.txt back\".\n\nLet me write the final response now. Keep intro/answers before the code, and a short \"what each outcome means\" after. Don't over-explain.",
