          "text": "Both answers, then the experiment that settles the first one.\n\n**On temp: yes, your instinct is right — temp 0 makes the retry a parrot by construction.** Greedy decoding shown its own answer and told \"fix this\" re-completes what it sees: the highest-probability continuation of \"here is your code\" is your code. Sampling is the *only* way to get a different answer from the same prompt (same seed + temp 0 = byte-identical call; that's why the echoes reproduced perfectly). But diversity ≠ correctness: a 3B at temp>0 also samples worse bodies more often, and every sample still has to clear the same gate + review. So rather than guess, here's a sweep that measures it — on the two cases we have exact repair prompts for (search, return), with the fill loop's own acceptance as scoreboard. I also threw in the variable your question implies: **show the refused answer vs. don't** — the echo may be an anchoring artifact of the prompt shape, not only of greedy sampling.\n\n**On prompt tightness: no — and the evidence says wording can't promise it.** Class by class:\n\n- *Closed:* invented API names (`models.date_today`, fake exceptions, run 3). Fix B + the refusal gate killed that class — run 4 had zero. The refusal regex is a hard gate there, not a probability.\n- *Open, and provably not wording:* the field invention (`record.author` when the field list was in the prompt), the contract miss (return shape), and gap-filling (14-day loan). The proof: the repair complaint quoted the violated fact **verbatim** — \"Book has no field `author` (fields: id, title, isbn, published_year, available_copies, author_id)\", \"declared `-> models.Loan`\" — and the model re-emitted the defect unchanged. Wording shifts probabilities; it doesn't buy capability.\n- *One more line that could target observed defects:* two fact-level gaps remain — cross-table joins (reading `Author` for names, not `record.author`) and what `create_*`/`update_*` return (the live borrow defect is exactly that gap: store `add` returns the record with its assigned id; the model returned the pre-save local). Those are pending decisions, and I'd gate them behind this sweep plus the expenses data — a bigger model may make both moot.\n\n**The sweep.** 8 cells: {anchored (shows refused answer, today's behavior), bare (complaints only)} × {0.0, 0.4, 0.8, 1.0}, seed fixed at `FALLBACK_SEED + 1` so every cell is deterministic and reproducible. Each cell runs a full `fill_stubs` on a pristine mechanical copy at `/tmp/library_sweep` — **out/library is never touched**. Note `anchored@0.0` is exactly the live call, so it must reproduce the echo: that's the control. Dry-run on the server passed (mechanical regen OK, bare-transform byte-equal to `previous=None`, model load cached across cells). From the repo root on the Mac:\n\n```bash\ncat > /tmp/temp_sweep.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Does the retry ever engage? Sweep sampling on the two known echoes.\n\nSetup: a pristine mechanical copy of out/library (/tmp/library_sweep),\nregenerated without --model — the same tree the real pass starts from.\nfill_stubs then runs once per cell with a wrapper around\nrunner.generate_free:\n\n  - ordinary asks go to the model exactly as in the real pass (temperature\n    0, the run's seed); the search and return first answers reproduce, so\n    both get refused and each gets one repair ask;\n  - the two repair asks (search, return) are answered with the cell's\n    sampling: variant \"anchored\" shows the refused answer back (what the\n    real pass does), variant \"bare\" removes that block (complaints only),\n    temperature is the cell's, and the seed is the run's + 1.\n\nScoring is fill_stubs' own gate: a cell where a repair lands prints\n\"written — repaired: ...\"; a refused one prints the complaints it still\nbroke. Nothing here touches out/library. Run from the repo root:\n\n    python3.12 -u /tmp/temp_sweep.py ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \".\")\n\nimport generator  # noqa: E402\nfrom kernel.extraction import runner  # noqa: E402\n\nMODEL = (sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1\n         else \"../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf\")\nSWEEP = \"/tmp/library_sweep\"\nNAMES = (\"repositories.py\", \"services.py\", \"models.py\", \"errors.py\",\n         \"store.py\")\nCASES = {\n    \"BookRepository.search_books_by_title_author_isbn\": \"search\",\n    \"LibraryService.return_book\": \"return\",\n    \"LibraryService.borrow_book\": \"borrow\",\n}\nMEASURED = {\"stub:BookRepository.search_books_by_title_author_isbn:repair\":\n            \"search\",\n            \"stub:LibraryService.return_book:repair\": \"return\"}\n\nshutil.rmtree(SWEEP, ignore_errors=True)\nshutil.copytree(\"out/library\", SWEEP)\ncode = generator.main([SWEEP])\nassert code == 0, f\"mechanical regen refused with {code}\"\nrequirements = generator.load_requirements(SWEEP)\n\n\ndef mechanical():\n    files = {}\n    for name in NAMES:\n        with open(os.path.join(SWEEP, \"generated\", name),\n                  encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n            files[name] = handle.read()\n    return files\n\n\nreal_generate = runner.generate_free\nreal_load = runner.load_model\n_loaded = {}\n\n\ndef cached_load(model_path, **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"One model instance for all cells; generate_free resets per call.\"\"\"\n    if \"llm\" not in _loaded:\n        print(f\"[sweep] loading {os.path.basename(model_path)} once\")\n        _loaded[\"llm\"] = real_load(model_path, **kwargs)\n    return _loaded[\"llm\"]\n\n\nrunner.load_model = cached_load\nCELL = {\"variant\": \"anchored\", \"temperature\": 0.0,\n        \"seed\": generator.FALLBACK_SEED + 1}\n\n\ndef bare_prompt(prompt):\n    \"\"\"The anchored repair prompt with the refused-answer block removed.\"\"\"\n    marker = \"\\n\\nThe refused answer was:\\n```python\\n\"\n    tail = (\"\\n```\\nWrite the body again, fixing exactly what was refused \"\n            \"and\\nkeeping what was right.\")\n    start = prompt.index(marker)\n    stop = prompt.index(tail, start) + len(tail)\n    return prompt[:start] + prompt[stop:]\n\n\ndef sweeper(llm, prompt, label, temperature=0.0, seed=None, **kwargs):\n    if label in MEASURED:\n        case = MEASURED[label]\n        if CELL[\"variant\"] == \"bare\":\n            prompt = bare_prompt(prompt)\n        print(f\"\\n[sweep] {case}: variant={CELL['variant']} \"\n              f\"temp={CELL['temperature']} seed={CELL['seed']}\")\n        result = real_generate(llm, prompt, label,\n                               temperature=CELL[\"temperature\"],\n                               seed=CELL[\"seed\"])\n        print(f\"[sweep] {case} answer:\\n{result.text.strip()}\\n\")\n        return result\n    print(f\"[ask]   {label}\")\n    return real_generate(llm, prompt, label, temperature=temperature,\n                         seed=seed)\n\n\nrunner.generate_free = sweeper\n\nRUNS = [(\"anchored\", 0.0), (\"anchored\", 0.4), (\"anchored\", 0.8),\n        (\"anchored\", 1.0), (\"bare\", 0.0), (\"bare\", 0.4), (\"bare\", 0.8),\n        (\"bare\", 1.0)]\nsummary = []\nfor variant, temperature in RUNS:\n    CELL[\"variant\"] = variant\n    CELL[\"temperature\"] = temperature\n    print(f\"\\n##### cell: variant={variant} temp={temperature} \"\n          f\"seed={CELL['seed']}\")\n    rows = generator.fill_stubs(mechanical(), MODEL, requirements,\n                                out=lambda _line: None)\n    outcomes = {}\n    for label, status, note in rows:\n        print(f\"  {label}: {status}{' — ' + note if note else ''}\")\n        if label in CASES:\n            outcomes[CASES[label]] = status\n    summary.append(((variant, temperature), outcomes))\n\nprint(\"\\n=== summary: per-cell outcome\")\nfor (variant, temperature), outcomes in summary:\n    line = \" | \".join(f\"{case}: {outcomes.get(case, '-')}\"\n                      for case in (\"search\", \"return\", \"borrow\"))\n    print(f\"  {variant:9s} temp={temperature}: {line}\")\nPY\n\ncaffeinate python3.12 -u /tmp/temp_sweep.py ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf 2>&1 | tee /tmp/sweep_out.txt\n```\n\nWhat the outcome buys us:\n\n- **A cell writes and the printed body reads right** → wire that (variant, temperature, seed offset) into `fill_stubs`' retry: one repair ask as now, but sampled; still deterministic per prompt. Note \"passed the gate\" ≠ correct — I'll want to read the body before wiring.\n- **Nothing engages across all 8** → the echo is capability, not sampling. Then the answer to \"raise temp?\" is no, the repair loop keeps its refusal/keep-stub/dump value, and the money goes to the model upgrade. `anchored@0.0` reproducing the echoes exactly confirms the harness is faithful.\n\nRuntime: one model load, then ~7 short generations per cell — roughly 15–25 minutes. Run from the repo root; paste `/tmp/sweep_out.txt` back (whole file — the echoed answers matter as much as the verdicts). Expenses r4 stays queued; I'd read the sweep first, so if we wire a winner, the expenses run exercises the new retry in the same session."
