ed as searchable text. |\n| bare@0.0 return | updates loan via `update_loan`, returns it | never increments `available_copies` — the returned copy stays unavailable (silent stock leak). |\n\n(`bare@0.8` search came back as two code blocks plus prose → refused; `bare@1.0` search used unbound `author`/`isbn`/`r` → refused.) Four of the five failures are *silent* ones — passing the gate, compiling, and misbehaving.\n\n## 3. Two gate candidates, each with a fresh specimen\n\n- **Class-scope `self.` names.** `_body_refusal` checks `self.<name>` against `_module_names(text)` — every 4-space name in the *whole module*. So a `BookRepository` body may call `self.read_one_author` because `AuthorRepository` defines it. Fix: collect names per class (plus `_store`/`_repos`), pass the stub's class in. Would have refused the bare@0.0 search body.\n- **`create_*/update_*` result discarded.** The parked sixth check, now with a second specimen: anchored@1.0's `updated_book = update_book(...)` is assigned, never read, and the pre-save local returned — the same family as the live borrow defect (`created = create_loan(...)` discarded). The parked wording just needs to cover `update_*` results too.\n\nNeither is implemented — say the word and I'll add them with regression tests (the two sweep bodies above are ready-made fixtures).\n\n## 4. New document finding (not about code — about the extraction)\n\n`invariants.json` says *\"Loan.return_date must be after Loan.due_date if Loan.status is 'returned'\"*, `errors.json` says `InvalidReturnDateError` fires when a book \"is returned before its due date\", and `service_contracts.json` lists that error for `return_book`. **None of this is in `prompt_library_system.txt`** — no return-validity rule exists in the source. The extraction fabricated a self-consistent constraint, and it's unsatisfiable: enforcing it would make every on-time return raise, contradicting requirements line 13 (\"sets return_date, updates status, increments copies\"). The