't in `BODY_IMPORTS`). So 4/5 produced guard-passing code; they're just intermediate versions, not the model's final one.\n\n## The repair ask was impossible\n\nThe repair prompt embeds the whole raw first answer (`previous=first_answer`, generator.py:3537):\n\n- repo stub: **34,259 chars** → over the 8192 context; the 41-char \"repair\" `def search_books_by_title_author_isbn` is exactly the shape of a `MIN_BUDGET=16`-token clamp;\n- services: ~26,000 chars → little or no room left, so those repairs were cut too.\n\nPer the settled decision I won't make the repair bare — but it should quote the **cleaned body** that was actually judged, not 16k chars of chain-of-thought.\n\n## Next: one probe settles the framing question\n\nWritten and syntax-checked: `/tmp/opencode/qwen_chat_probe.py` (md5 `f95b72ae9a1c6ea489eedd7e32327fc2`). From the Mac, repo root:\n\n```bash\nscp gstenger@vmi1620255.contaboserver.net:/tmp/opencode/qwen_chat_probe.py /tmp/opencode/\ncaffeinate python3.12 /tmp/opencode/qwen_chat_probe.py ../models/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-Q4_K_M.gguf\n```\n\nIt builds the real borrow stub prompt, prints `general.name` and the chat template (so we know the file really is the non-thinking 2507 Instruct), the measured prompt/repair token counts, and answers four ways at temp 0, seed 20261012: raw @3584, raw @full room, chat (user), chat (system+user). If chat returns a few hundred tokens of code while raw fills the budget, the \"thinking\" is the raw-completion framing, and chat is the lever.\n\nAfter that I'd patch the harness (continuation-aware fence parse; truncation = refusal + one full-room retry, with `finish_reason`/tokens in the dump; repair quotes the cleaned body; dump the first complaints too — today kept rows only store the repair's). Want me to start on that patch now, or wait for the probe output?"
