      "summary": "## Objective\n- Drive the LLM architecture-extraction pipeline (prompts → JSON docs → runnable Python) to zero generator blockers; current focus is the model-scale A/B (Ministral-3B vs Qwen3-4B) on the library program, which this analysis just invalidated.\n\n## Requirements\n- `prompts/*.txt` frozen; JSON docs per prompt consistent (triage copies in `backup/prompts_triage/`).\n- Model runs on the Mac only; hand the user Mac commands; `caffeinate` for long runs; first asks use temp 0, seed 20261012.\n- No catalog additions; the generator must refuse blocked docs, never invent silently; human answers persist (`decisions.json`, `field_aliases.json`, `surface_decisions.json`, `method_slots.json`), prompt-hash stamped, re-applied on reruns.\n- `--quiet` on extract side; GUI via `generator.py --gui-tech`; generated `gui.py` portable; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`.\n- LLM pass lives in `generator.py`; answers checked manually; generated output is never pushed back; Mac-local hand fixes are discarded if regenerated (accepted).\n- Generated artifacts are evidence: do not edit `out/library` documents to \"fix\" findings.\n\n## Decisions\n- Repair loop committed `9a18c2f` (Mac pulled): one informed re-ask per failed stub; complaint text quoted; repaired bodies tagged `[llm-written — review]` and still counted as stubs; a body that still fails keeps the stub; dump gains `first_answer`/`complaints`.\n- **Retry temperature: no.** Sweep measured it; do not wire retry temperature and do not switch the repair prompt to `bare` (complaints without the refused answer). Keep anchored temp 0 — echo → `still refused` → stub stands is the safe failure mode at 3B. (Refinement proposed, not yet approved: repair should quote the *cleaned body* that was judged, not the raw transcript — still shows the refused answer.)\n- Anchor is the parrot-maker, not temperature: `anchored@0.0` vs `bare@0.0` (same greedy decoding) = echo vs engaged; `anchored@0.4` byte-identical to `anchored@0.0`.\n- Engagement ≠ correctness: 5 gate-passing repairs, 0 review-clean; most silently wrong. anchored@0.8 return fails the double-return bar and corrupts stock.\n- **Qwen3-4B library run verdict invalid:** `0 of 5` is a harness artifact — 4/5 first answers truncated at the 3584-token ceiling, the 5th (renew) lost to `extract_code`; do not read it as a model verdict.\n- Diagnosis accepted: \"thinking\" = raw completion without the GGUF chat template (runner calls `llm(prompt=...)` via `generate_free`), not the Qwen *thinking* variant; Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 is non-thinking and should answer directly under its chat template.\n- Two checker candidates still pending, not yet implemented: (a) class-scope `self.<name>` names; (b) generalize the parked create/update-result-discard check.\n- Document finding: return-date invariant / `InvalidReturnDateError` / contract `raises` entry are extraction fabrications absent from `prompts/prompt_library_system.txt` — log as a finding, leave documents frozen.\n- Carried: remaining defects are LLM quality; FILTER_CRITERION answers for parameterless filter stubs; dead CLI flags kept and reported; option-selected actions choose routes → alternates → fallback; `book list -author` and `expense report -yearly` stay findings.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Sparked by user's \"I think it's a 'thinking' problem\": Qwen3-4B run finished; dump copied to `/tmp/opencode/qwen4b_llm_stub_answers.json` (93,660 B) and fully analyzed.\n- All five refusals diagnosed as harness artifacts, not model code: 4/5 first answers cut mid-sentence at `MAX_NEW_TOKENS=3584`; the 41-char repo repair is the `MIN_BUDGET=16` clamp shape.\n- `extract_code` fence-parity bug found: prompt ends with an open ```python; the model's first ``` closes it; `re.findall` (generator.py:2817) reads that closing fence as an opener and captures the prose between fences. Complaints follow from prose: unterminated string, `invalid character '—'/'→'`, `calls self.