getRepository.export_widgets:retry\",\n                                  \"stub:WidgetService.custom_total\"])\n        self.assertEqual(chat.call_args_list[1].kwargs[\"max_new_tokens\"], 8128)\n        self.assertIn(\"raise NotImplementedError(\", files[\"repositories.py\"])\n        self.assertNotIn(\"[llm-written\", files[\"repositories.py\"])\n```\n\nHmm wait: `n_ctx()` = 8192, `tokenize` returns [] → available_tokens = 8128. First budget = min(3584, 8128)=3584. Good.\n\nBut careful: `Model` class attribute metadata is a dict; `has_chat_template` → True. Good.\n\nAlso the dump telemetry test: add `truncated`/`finish_reason`/`tokens`/`budget` assertions to the existing dump test, and a truncated-entry check. Let me extend `test_the_dump_records_both_attempts_when_repaired`:\n\n```python\n        self.assertEqual(data[0][\"status\"], \"written\")\n        self.assertEqual(data[0][\"finish_reason\"], \"stop\")\n        self.assertEqual(data[0][\"tokens\"], 3)\n        self.assertEqual(data[0][\"budget\"], 3584)\n        self.assertFalse(data[0][\"truncated\"])\n        self.assertEqual(data[0][\"first_finish_reason\"], \"stop\")\n        self.assertFalse(data[0][\"first_truncated\"])\n```\nAnd a new small dump test for a truncated row? Could fold into the truncation test with a dump_path. Let me add dump to the truncation test... The `fill` helper doesn't support dump_path. Let me extend the truncation test with tempfile dump:\n\nActually simpler: keep the truncation test as is; the dump keys are asserted in the repaired test. Add `\"first_truncated\"`/telemetry assertions there. Good enough.\n\nNow, also test the repair quotes the *body*: extend `test_the_repair_prompt_shows_the_refused_answer` with a wrapped answer? That test uses raw \"return None\" (body == raw). Add a new test:\n\n```python\n    def test_the_repair_ask_quotes_the_judged_body_not_the_raw_transcript(self):\n        \"\"\"The raw transcript that made the live repair ask overflow the\n        context is not what the complaints are about; the body is.\"\"\"\n        from unittest import mock\n        files, _stats = self.rendered()\n        first = (\"    def export_widgets(self, file_path: str = None) -> None:\\n\"\n                 '        \"\"\"Writes widgets.\"\"\"\\n'\n                 \"        raise NotImplementedError(\\n\"\n                 '            \"plain-method\")\\n'\n                 \"```\\n\"\n                 \"\\n\"\n                 \"Reasoning that is not the answer, with an em-dash.\\n\"\n                 \"\\n\"\n                 \"```python\\n\"\n                 \"return None\\n\"\n                 \"```\\n\")\n        replies = [\n            mock.Mock(text=first, tokens=30, seconds=0.1, budget=3584,\n                      finish_reason=\"stop\", truncated=False),\n            mock.Mock(text=\"handle = open(file_path, \\\"w\\\")\\n\"\n                           \"handle.close()\\nreturn None\",\n                      tokens=3, seconds=0.1, budget=3584,\n                      finish_reason=\"stop\", truncated=False),\n            mock.Mock(text=\"return 0\", tokens=3, seconds=0.1, budget=3584,\n                      finish_reason=\"stop\", truncated=False),\n        ]\n        with mock.patch.object(generator.runner, \"load_model\",\n                               return_value=object()), \\\n                mock.patch.object(generator.runner, \"generate_free\",\n                                  side_effect=replies) as ask:\n            generator.fill_stubs(files, \"fake.gguf\", \"requirements text\",\n                                 out=lambda _line: None)\n        repair = ask.call_args_list[1].args[1]\n        self.assertIn(\"The refused answer was:\", repair)\n        self.assertIn(\"return None\", repair)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"Reasoning that is not the answer\", repair)\n```\nWait: the first answer's extracted body = \"return None\" (the continuation parse: first region = echo (def...raise) → last python block = \"retu