                "text": "Create a multi-module Python library management system with the following features:\n\n1. **Book model** — id, title, isbn (unique), published_year, available_copies (default 1)\n2. **Author model** — id, name, birth_year, biography\n3. **Member model** — id, name, email (unique), membership_date, is_active (default True)\n4. **Loan model** — id, book_id (FK), member_id (FK), loan_date, due_date, return_date (nullable), status (active/returned/overdue)\n5. **BookRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + search by title/author/isbn + filtering by available copies\n6. **AuthorRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + find books by author\n7. **MemberRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + find active/inactive members\n8. **LoanRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + find active loans, overdue loans, member loan history, book loan history\n9. **LibraryService** — business logic:\n   - borrow_book(member_id, book_id): checks availability, creates loan, decrements copies\n   - return_book(loan_id): sets return_date, updates status, increments copies\n   - get_overdue_loans(): returns loans past due_date\n   - renew_membership(member_id): toggles is_active\n   - search_books(query): searches across title/author/isbn\n10. **CLI interface using click** with commands:\n   - `library book add --title --isbn --author-id --published-year --copies`\n   - `library book list [--author] [--available-only]`\n   - `library book search --query`\n   - `library member add --name --email`\n   - `library member list [--active-only]`\n   - `library borrow --member-id --book-id`\n   - `library return --loan-id`\n   - `library overdue`\n   - `library member history --member-id`\n\nUse type hints throughout. Use SQLite with foreign keys enabled. The database schema must enforce referential integrity with CASCADE deletes. Follow clean architecture with proper separation of concerns. All IDs must be auto-incremented primary keys that are optional (default None) in the domain models.\n---MODELS---\n\"\"\"Data models. Every field defaults to None: the store assigns integer\nprimary keys on insert, and updates merge only non-None values.\"\"\"\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nimport datetime\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional\n\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Book:\n    id: int = None\n    title: str = None\n    isbn: str = None\n    published_year: Optional[int] = None\n    available_copies: int = None\n    author_id: int = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Author:\n    id: int = None\n    name: str = None\n    birth_year: Optional[int] = None\n    biography: Optional[str] = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Member:\n    id: int = None\n    name: str = None\n    email: str = None\n    membership_date: datetime.date = None\n    is_active: bool = None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Loan:\n    id: int = None\n    book_id: int = None\n    member_id: int = None\n    loan_date: datetime.datetime = None\n    due_date: datetime.datetime = None\n    return_date: Optional[datetime.datetime] = None\n    status: str = None\n---ERRORS---\n\"\"\"Application errors, one class per registered failure.\"\"\"\n\n\n\nclass BookNotFoundError(LookupError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a book with the given ISBN or ID is not found in the database.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass AuthorNotFoundError(LookupError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an author with the given ID is not found in the database.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass MemberNotFoundError(LookupError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a member with the given ID is not found in the database.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass LoanNotFoundError(LookupError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a loan with the given ID is not found in the database.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass BookAlreadyExistsError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when attempting to add a book with an existing ISBN.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass MemberAlreadyExistsError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when attempting to add a member with an existing email.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientCopiesError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\