y does `sys.path.insert(0, dirname)`. The driver runs `[sys.executable, \"cli.py\", \"--db\", \"lab.db\"]` with cwd=GEN, so imports resolve.\n\nLet me create the smoke script based on drive_library4.py but with the new tree and tests that expose the defects. I'll write it to /tmp/opencode/qwen_chat_smoke.py and run it locally.\n\nKey checks:\nA. `book search -query earthsea` (title) → works.\nB. `book search -query \"le guin\"` (author) → service crash (AttributeError). This proves the defect.\nC. `book search -query 978-1` (ISBN) → service crash (same).\nD. repo search directly for author and ISBN → author works, ISBN fails (returns []) — to isolate the repo defect from the service defect.\nE. borrow twice:\n   - borrow 1 1 → success.\n   - count loans.\n   - borrow 1 1 again → error; count loans → 2 (a loan was created before the availability failure). Proof of corruption.\nF. return 1 → success; book copies back to 1; status returned; return_date set.\nG. return 1 again → InvalidReturnDateError (wrong error, but at least no double increment).\nH. renew direct: toggles twice; check the updated member.\n\nLet me write and run.",
