          "text": "Honest run: **5/5 written, one repair — the API facts fixed the API failures, the remaining defects are logic and types.**\n\nTelemetry: all `stop`, 144–179 tokens, no truncation. The repo prompt's answer budget drops to 3,044 because the prompt is larger.\n\n**What the facts fixed**\n- No invented error names; every `errors.*` reference is defined.\n- Every repository call exists — the phantom-method class is gone.\n- Dates are `datetime` objects, not epoch ints or space-formatted strings.\n- `renew_membership` is clean and persists via `update_member`.\n\n**What still fails (smoke, not import)**\n- `return_book`: fatal `AttributeError: 'Loan' object has no attribute 'title'`. It tries to build a `models.Book` out of loan fields, so the loan is never updated: status stays `active`, `return_date` stays `None`, copies unchanged. The dump's `first_answer` shows the same construction in the first attempt — the repair fixed only the return value, not the confusion. It also raises `LoanNotFoundError` for an inactive loan.\n- `borrow_book`: happy path works, but it creates the loan **before** reading/checking the book. Borrowing a zero-copy book raises `InsufficientCopiesError` and leaves a phantom active loan (loans 1→2). The 14-day due date is still invented; no member/`is_active` check.\n- Both searches: title and author work, ISBN returns `[]` for authored books — the explicit \"independent fields, not `elif`\" rule did not change the model's behavior. The service search duplicates the repo logic instead of delegating.\n\n**Prompt comparison**\n\n| run | written | clean on smoke | failure class |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| full | 5/5 | 2/5 | wrong error names, phantom loan, service crash |\n| minimal | 2/5 | 0/2 | undefined errors, phantom methods |\n| honest | 5/5 | 1/5 | logic/type errors, all APIs real |\n\nThe honest prompt did its job: it removed the refusal and invented-API class. It did not make Qwen reason correctly about ordering, model identity, or multi-field matching.\n\n**Two checks this run strengthens**\n- **(d) write-before-raise**: now seen in both full and honest borrow bodies, with a real consequence (phantom loan). Strong go.\n- **(c) typed receiver**: `loan.title` is invisible today because the typed map only learns `models.X(...)` assignments. `loan` comes from `read_one_loan() -> models.Loan`; teaching the map repository return types would catch both this and the full run's `book.author_id.lower()`.\n\n**A/B — Ministral on the same honest prompt:**\n```\ncaffeinate python3.12 generator.py /tmp/library_repair --model ../models/Ministral-3-3B-Instruct-2512-Q4_K_M.gguf --stub-context honest\n```\n```\nscp /tmp/library_repair/llm_stub_answers.json /tmp/library_repair/generated/*.py gstenger@vmi1620255.contaboserver.net:/tmp/opencode/library_ministral_honest/\n```\n\nLanding dir is ready. I'll review and smoke it the same way, then put the two transcripts side by side."
