, io, random, string, collections, itertools, functools, decimal, uuid, datetime, pathlib, sqlite3\n\nrequirements:\nCreate a multi-module Python library management system with the following features:\n\n1. **Book model** — id, title, isbn (unique), published_year, available_copies (default 1)\n2. **Author model** — id, name, birth_year, biography\n3. **Member model** — id, name, email (unique), membership_date, is_active (default True)\n4. **Loan model** — id, book_id (FK), member_id (FK), loan_date, due_date, return_date (nullable), status (active/returned/overdue)\n5. **BookRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + search by title/author/isbn + filtering by available copies\n6. **AuthorRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + find books by author\n7. **MemberRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + find active/inactive members\n8. **LoanRepository** — SQLite storage with CRUD + find active loans, overdue loans, member loan history, book loan history\n9. **LibraryService** — business logic:\n   - borrow_book(member_id, book_id): checks availability, creates loan, decrements copies\n   - return_book(loan_id): sets return_date, updates status, increments copies\n   - get_overdue_loans(): returns loans past due_date\n   - renew_membership(member_id): toggles is_active\n   - search_books(query): searches across title/author/isbn\n10. **CLI interface using click** with commands:\n   - `library book add --title --isbn --author-id --published-year --copies`\n   - `library book list [--author] [--available-only]`\n   - `library book search --query`\n   - `library member add --name --email`\n   - `library member list [--active-only]`\n   - `library borrow --member-id --book-id`\n   - `library return --loan-id`\n   - `library overdue`\n   - `library member history --member-id`\n\nUse type hints throughout. Use SQLite with foreign keys enabled. The database schema must enforce referential integrity with CASCADE deletes. Follow clean architecture with proper separation of concerns. All IDs must be auto-incremented primary keys that are optional (default None) in the domain models.\n\nmodule (services.py):\n```python\n\"\"\"Services. A method with the same name as a repository method delegates\nto it; anything else raises NotImplementedError with its work order.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Union\n\nimport calendar\n\nimport models\nimport errors\nfrom store import match_criterion\n\n\ndef _holds(actual, operator, expected):\n    \"\"\"Twin of `store._holds`: the operators filter composition reuses.\"\"\"\n    if operator == \"eq\":\n        return actual == expected\n    if operator == \"ge\":\n        return actual is not None and actual >= expected\n    if operator == \"le\":\n        return actual is not None and actual <= expected\n    raise ValueError(f\"unknown operator {operator!r}\")\n\n\n\nclass LibraryService:\n\n    def __init__(self, repos):\n        self._repos = repos\n\n\n    def borrow_book(self, member_id: int = None, book_id: int = None) -> models.Loan:\n        \"\"\"Borrow a book by member and book IDs, checks availability, creates loan, and decrements copies. [rule plain-method: method needs custom logic]\"\"\"\n        raise NotImplementedError(\n            \"LibraryService.borrow_book: rule plain-method: method needs custom logic\")\n\n    def return_book(self, loan_id: int = None) -> models.Loan:\n        \"\"\"Returns a book by loan ID, sets return_date, updates status, and increments copies. [pattern STANDARD_CRUD: no mechanical reading]\"\"\"\n        raise NotImplementedError(\n            \"LibraryService.return_book: pattern STANDARD_CRUD: no mechanical reading\")\n\n    def get_overdue_loans(self) -> List[models.Loan]:\n        \"\"\"Returns all overdue loans. [delegates to LoanRepository.get_overdue_loans — pattern realized by target]\"\"\"\n        return self._repos['LoanRepository'].get_overdue_loans()\n\n    def renew_membership(self, member_id: int = None) -> models.Member:\n        \"\"\"Renews membership by toggling is_active status. [llm-written by Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-Q4_K_M.gguf — review]\"\"\"\n        member = self._repos['MemberRepository'].read_one_member(member_id)\n        if member is None:\n            raise errors.MemberNotFoundError(member_id)\n        member.is_active = not member.is_active\n        updated_member = self._repos['MemberRepository'].update_member(member_id, member)\n        return updated_member\n\n    def search_books(self, query: str = None) -> List[models.Book]:\n        \"\"\"Searches books by title, author, or ISBN. [llm-written by Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-Q4_K_M.gguf — review]\"\"\"\n        results = []\n        if query is None:\n            return results\n\n        books = self._repos['BookRepository'].read_all_books()\n        author_books = self._repos['AuthorRepository'].read_all_authors()\n        author_id_map = {author.id: author.name for author in author_books}\n\n        for book in books:\n            if book.title and query.lower() in book.title.lower():\n                results.append(book)\n            elif book.author_id and book.author_id in author_id_map:\n                author_name = author_id_map[book.author_id]\n                if query.lower() in author_name.lower():\n                    results.append(book)\n            elif book.isbn and query.lower() in book.isbn.lower():\n                results.append(book)\n\n        return results\n```\n\nNow write the body of `LibraryService.return_book`, replacing\nthe `raise NotImplementedError(...)` statement:\n```python\n````\n\nTwo things worth noting about this exact text:\n\n- `renew_membership` and `search_books` are already written into the module by the time this ask is made; `borrow_book` is still stubbed after it.\n- The repair ask (11,864 chars) is this same prompt plus the complaint and the refused first body. Say the word if you want that one too."
