          "text": "**Verdict: not a clean Qwen base.** The borrow guard worked, but the return regressed. I did not start Ministral.\n\n## Findings\n\n**Borrow — kept (correct refusal, still a blocker)**\n- First answer: `create_loan(...)` before the book check/raises.\n- Repair: moves to `read_one_book` → checks → `update_book` → `create_loan(...)`.\n- The `update_*`-before-`create_*` guard caught it and kept the stub. No wrong body landed, but the requirement line still did not stop Qwen from reordering the repair.\n\n**Return — written but wrong**\nThe new body:\n- sets `loan.return_date = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(loan.due_date)` twice, instead of using the return time;\n- never reads or updates the book, so `available_copies` does not increase;\n- sets status and calls `update_loan` correctly.\n\nSmoke confirms:\n```text\nreturn_date == due_date: True\ncopies after: 1 (expected 2)\n```\nThis is a regression from the previous exact run, where the final block had the correct return. The added requirement line produced a single 10-line answer with no final block, and `_body_complaints` has neither the requirement line nor a `return_date`/`due_date` fact, so it accepted the body.\n\n**Search — functionally correct, but messy**\nRepository search covers title/author/ISBN and the smoke passes all three. The service adds a dead author loop that passes an author *name* into `find_books_by_author(author_id=...)`, and calls the repository search twice. Results are still correct because the first repo call already found the author match. Not a blocker, but worth a later cleanup.\n\n**Renew — correct per spec**\nThe requirement literally says “toggles is_active,” so `True → False` is not a regression.\n\n## Next fixes\n\n1. **Return guard in `generator.py`**\n   - Pass `_requirements_line(...)` into `_body_complaints` from `fill_stubs`.\n   - If the requirement says `increments copies` / `decrements copies`, require the body to touch the copies field and update a Book.\n   - Refuse `return_date` assigned from `due_date`.\n   - Add tests; the repair ask then gets concrete complaints.\n\n2. **Borrow repair order**\n   - Make the create-before-raise complaint explicit: “validate first, create the loan, then decrement/update the book.”\n   - Optionally add the same ordered steps to the target contract.\n   - Keep the update-before-create guard.\n\n3. **Rerun Qwen exact on the same docs, smoke, then compare Ministral.**\n\nI’m holding Ministral until the return and borrow rerun. If you want, I’ll implement the return guard and the stronger borrow complaint now."
