          "text": "Now add helper functions `_target_field_name`, `_assignment_targets`, `_field_writes`, `_call_attrs`, `_contract_complaints` before `_add_imports`.\n\nLet's design code carefully.\n\n```\ndef _node_field_name(node):\n    if isinstance(node, ast.Attribute): return node.attr\n    if isinstance(node, ast.Subscript):\n        sl = node.slice\n        if isinstance(sl, ast.Constant) and isinstance(sl.value, str): return sl.value\n        if isinstance(sl, ast.Index)... Python 3.12 ast.Index? Not needed.\n    return None\n\ndef _assignment_targets(node):\n    if isinstance(node, ast.Assign): return node.targets, node.value\n    if isinstance(node, ast.AnnAssign) and node.value is not None: return [node.target], node.value\n    if isinstance(node, ast.AugAssign): return [node.target], node.value\n    return [], None\n\ndef _writes_field(tree, field):\n    out=[]\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        targets, value = _assignment_targets(node)\n        if any(_node_field_name(t)==field for t in targets):\n            out.append((node,value))\n    return out\n\ndef _mentions_field(node, field):\n    return any(_node_field_name(inner)==field for inner in ast.walk(node))\n```\n- `_node_field_name` for `augassign.target`; for `Assign.targets` may be tuple? The target itself. We can handle `ast.Tuple`/List by walking elements? The model likely direct. Add:\n```\nif isinstance(node,(ast.Tuple, ast.List)): return any(...) for elements? \n```\nBetter `_target_fields(target)` returns set:\n```\ndef _target_fields(target):\n  if isinstance(target,(ast.Tuple, ast.List)): union\n  name = _node_field_name; return {name} or set()\n```\nUse in `_field_writes`.\n- `_call_attrs(tree)`:\n```\nreturn {node.func.attr for node in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(node, ast.Call) and isinstance(node.func, ast.Attribute)}\n```\n- `_raise_names(tree)`: `_raised_name` exists; set.\n- `_last_name(value)`: `value.rsplit(\".\",1)[-1]`.\n- `_effect_complaints`:\n```\nfor item in contract.get(\"effects\") or []:\n  target = item[\"target\"]; field=_last_name; writes=_field_writes(tree, field)\n  if not writes: complaint...\n  op = item[\"op\"]\n  if op in (\"increment\",\"decrement\"):\n     op_type = ast.Add if increment else ast.Sub\n     matching = any(_has_op(node, value, target, op_type) ...)\n```\nDo we enforce op? Let's implement `_has_op`:\n```\ndef _arithmetic_matches(target_fields, value, op_type):\n  if isinstance(node, ast.AugAssign) and is op_type: True\n  if isinstance(node, ast.Assign) and isinstance(value, ast.BinOp) and isinstance(value.op, op_type):\n      # one side mentions the target field\n      if any(_mentions_field(side, field) for side in (value.left, value.right)): True\n```\nFor `AugAssign`, the target field matches. The `writes` list nodes; check.\n- If op set, any.\n- If op increment/decrement and no matching, complaint: `\"the contract says increment `{target}`, but the body does not increment it\"`. The model's return body uses `+=`; fine. The Qwen borrow repair uses `-=`; fine. The first answer uses `-=`; fine.\n- The body could use `book.available_copies = book.available_copies - 1`; BinOp Sub; match.\n- The body could use `new = book.available_copies - 1; book.available_copies = new`; no match -> complaint. The model likely not. Fine.\n- The `by` value not checked.\n- The write call:\n```\nif item.get(\"write\"):\n   name=_last_name(write)\n   if name not in _call_attrs(tree): complaint\n```\n  - The write may be `self._store.update` -> last \"update\"; body calls. If the body calls `update_book` but the contract write `BookRepository.update_book`; last. Good.\n  - The `write` may include parentheses? The review stores no. Fine.\n- The value now:\n```\nif op == \"set\" and str(item.get(\"value\",\"\")).lower() == \"now\":\n   if not any(\"now\" in _call_attrs(inner) for ... writes)? \n```\n  - `_call_attrs` for the whole tree includes `now`; require. But if the body writes the field from `due_date` and also calls `.now()` for something else, false pass; the forbid. Good.\n  - The `write` RHS assignment `loan.return_date = datetime.datetime.now()`; `now` in call attrs. Good.\n- The forbid:\n```\nfor rule:\n  tfield=_last_name(target), rfield=_last_name(reads)\n  for node, value in _field_writes(tree, tfield):\n      if value is not None and _mentions_field(value, rfield):\n          found.append(rule.get(\"message\") or f\"`{target}` is set from `{reads}`; the contract forbids it\")\n          break\n```\n  - The wrong return_date body uses `datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(loan.due_date)`; `_mentions_field` finds due_date. Good.\n  - The current correct body sets now; no.\n- Creates:\n```\nfor item in creates:\n  call=item.get(\"call\")\n  if call:\n     name=_last_name(call)\n     if name not in _call_attrs: complaint\n```\n  - The body may call `create_loan`; yes.\n  - The class maybe; no check.\n- Preconditions:\n```\nfor item in preconditions:\n  error=item.get(\"error\")\n  if error:\n     name=_last_name(error)\n     if name not in _raise_names: complaint\n```\n  - The body may `raise errors.MemberNotFoundError`; `_raised_name` returns MemberNotFoundError. Good.\n  - The body may `raise MemberNotFoundError` no errors prefix; AST Name; returns. Good.\n- The `order` not checked; generic.\n- The contract checks should not run if contract is None. `_contract_complaints` returns [].\n- The error messages are human, generic. Use the target names from contract. No domain.\n- Add `found.extend(_contract_complaints(...))` after all generic checks; the generic `fields` variable is available. Good.\n- The `_contract_complaints` needs the `tree`; no `fields`. Good.\n\nLet's add.",
