      "summary": "## Objective\n- Make stub-fill correct and domain-general: move app-specific behavior into human-owned contracts, then establish a clean Qwen exact baseline and compare Ministral on the same harness.\n\n## Requirements\n- Domain-specific behavior (library return/borrow, copies, dates) must not be hardcoded in `generator.py`; the same engine must support factory/stock management.\n- `prompts/*.txt` are frozen; JSON docs stay consistent with `backup/prompts_triage/`.\n- Model runs on the Mac only, under `caffeinate`; temp 0 and seed 20261012 for first asks.\n- No catalog additions; generator refuses blocked docs and never invents silently; human answers persist prompt-hash stamped.\n- `--quiet` on extract side; GUI via `generator.py --gui-tech`; generated `gui.py` portable; unmet patterns stay `NotImplementedError`.\n- Generated artifacts are evidence: never edit `out/library` documents to fix findings.\n- Accepted bodies stay tagged `[llm-written — review]` and counted as stubs; judge by reading/running.\n- Experiment order: V3 minimal, V2 honest, exact; add only what a failure proves missing.\n- Prompt remains user-only: no system prompt, persona, or `enable_thinking`.\n- 14-day loan period accepted for now; add a fact checker in `extract_arch.py` later, not the generator.\n- Clean Qwen base before Ministral; both use the same harness.\n- No restore between runs; `main` re-renders `generated/` and overwrites the dump.\n\n## Decisions\n- Agreed: the library-specific rules added to `_target_contract`/`_body_complaints` are overfit and must be removed from code.\n- Direction: human-owned `method_contracts.json` with preconditions/effects/creates/order/forbid, `decided_by: user` + `requirements_sha`; `extract_arch.py` proposes/asks; generator compiles/checks generically; missing/stale facts keep the stub as `[needs_contract]`. Schema/location not yet approved.\n- Keep generic guards: typed reads, inline import allowlist, create-before-raise, update-bef